re going to be diving in Texas tonight on the, next to the border as well. And it's defined very differently depending on where you are in the country. But I do want to dive in Miami-Dade because you're, these numbers are very telling and it backs up what Maria Elena just said.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look, this is stunning for anyone who's watched Florida politics over the years.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIAMI-DADE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMINGS: 44.9%; RUBIO: 54.2%\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For Miami to go red by 10 points, for Marco Rubio to win by 60,000 votes, keep in mind, Joe Biden two years ago in the county, he got 53% of the vote. He lost Florida. He still got 53% of the vote in Miami-Dade County. And the fact that Marco Rubio is running up the numbers, Rachel's got the numbers up for Ron DeSantis. They're very similar, double-digit win in Miami.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, really blown away here by just how much DeSantis is outperforming where former President Donald Trump was in the bedrock, right, the Democratic bedrock in Florida. Not only here, but also take a look in Orlando, in Orange as well.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ORANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRIST: 52.8%; DESANTIS: 46.3%\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Former President Donald Trump, 37% of the vote back in 2020, look at Ron DeSantis, 46% of the vote.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You had just today, Donald Trump in that interview warning, if you will, Ron DeSantis not to run for now, otherwise he could be hurt by running.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. And look, and he is, you talk to people close to Trump and they will tell you that he is ready to come down hard on Ron DeSantis. But how do you do that now? Ron DeSantis just won decisively re-election in Florida despite the fact that Donald Trump never endorsed him. Di