publican candidates outside DC and in Virginia are using his playbook.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was with the Governor Youngkin as he was campaigning for Yesli Vega running against Spanberger. The playbook is, basically, Donald Trump's policies, you know, very conservative, but without the drama of Donald Trump and not really embracing Donald Trump. There's another important point here, though. Kevin McCarthy, the presumptive speaker if Republicans win, has gone out to recruit candidates in these races. And he's had a priority here, to recruit women, to recruit minorities and to recruit veterans. And in these races, what have you seen, two women, one of them also a veteran and one of them also a Latina. So, this has been McCarthy's strategy, because he noted that, in 2020, Republicans picked up seats, picked up 20 seats. Every Republican that knocked off a Democrat was a woman. So, that's, we may be seeing some of that strategy also there.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And gain, they only need five seats for Republicans to take back control of the House. Cecilia Vega, what is the relationship between President Biden and Kevin McCarthy? Is there one? Yeah, there you go.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ooh. Where do we begin? There is not one. There's not much of one. Kevin McCarthy hasn't been to the White House in a very long time. There's reportedly was one phone call to the White House from Kevin McCarthy. He had to get patched through. They had to call back to confirm that it was him. But look, Kevin McCarthy has said he doesn't necessarily want to launch all of these investigations that many or impeachment, at least challenges that Republicans in his party or caucus are calling for if, in fact, they take control. But remember, President Biden won this office because he campaigned on being someone who could work on both sides of the aisle.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is going to be the biggest challenge for him going forward after tonight, depending on what happens on whether he can continue to keep that promise going, given that he does not have very much of a relationship with the potential future speaker of the House.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the biggest challenge for Kevin McCarthy is what the Republican House looks like if they, in fact, gain back control of the House. What the makeup is if he has a fractious party or whether or not if he has moderate Republicans like he is or he has to make some deals in order, we've heard a lot about Marjorie Taylor Green, for example, who would return to a committee post.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is not going to be easy for Republican leadership to try and corral what was going to be a lot likely going to be a lot of very Trump-leaning members of Congress. And, of course, we have seen Kevin McCarthy fall right in line with Donald Trump. He is a big supporter of his. You know, he broke with him very, very, very briefly right after January 6th, turned right back to him.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But in an important moment, he came out and held him accountable for it.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. Yes. But how he is going to respond, how is he going to corral this group of Republicans, which is likely to include, yes, some more establishment Republicans, but increasingly a lot of very MAGA Republicans? And if the Senate flips, that's a whole other conversation of challenges over there.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. How does he do it, Jon Karl, Kevin McCarthy? People don't realize that he's been hopscotching the country and he's a campaigner, and he's been helping so many of these Republican candidates. Is he ready? Is he, does he have the formula down based on what the makeup is of the House at the end of the 