APHICS: KATIE BRITT, PROJECTED WINNER\par \par \uc2 KYRA PHILLIPS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Right now, we can tell you, ABC News projects the Republican Katie Britt has won the Senate race in Alabama. She'll become the first woman to ever be elected to the Senate from Alabama.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR: SOUTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOE CUNNINGHAM: 41.8%; HENRY MCMASTER: 57.1%\par \par \uc2 KYRA PHILLIPS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And in South Carolina, we are projecting that incumbent Republican Henry McMaster has been re-elected as governor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR: NEW HAMPSHIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOM SHERMAN: 46.7%; CHRIS SUNUNU: 52.7%\par \par \uc2 KYRA PHILLIPS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And ABC also can project that Republican incumbent Governor Chris Sununu has won his re-election bid in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 KYRA PHILLIPS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, to other headlines quickly, Ukraine's President suggesting he would be open to peace talks with Russia, softening his prior stance, refusing to negotiate while Vladimir Putin is in power. Zelenskyy calling for the international community to force Russia into real peace talks with demands that all occupied lands are returned to Ukraine. The balance of power in Congress could affect how much future US aid is given to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 KYRA PHILLIPS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the January 6th committee interviewed the driver of former President Trump's vehicle on January 6th. That interview taking place with committee investigators yesterday. We're going to have a lot more news ahead on this election night. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2022\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back, as we hit the top of the hour. 9:00 here in the east, 6:00 PM in the west and the polls have just closed in 15 more states, including here in New York, Arizona, Michigan, Texas, and now Wisconsin, several key states there. The polls now closed in 41 states total, nine more states in the west still open. Let's run down the numbers as they come in. Take a look at the races we're following at this hour.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE: ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARK KELLY; BLAKE MASTERS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Arizona Senate race, of course, as soon as we get numbers on this they come in, Mark Kelly being challenged by Blake Masters.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR: ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KATIE HOBBS; KARI LAKE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Arizona governor race getting national attention, the Democrat, Katie Hobbs, the secretary of state there. Her challenger, Republican Kari Lake, a former television news anchor there in Phoenix, an election denier, Donald Trump backing her solidly. Jon Karl will be talking about Kari Lake here in a moment.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE: COLORADO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MICHAEL BENNET; JOE O'DEA\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) To Colorado we go. The senator there, the Democrat, Michael Bennet, seeking a third term, hoping to return to the Senate, up against a moderate Republican, Joe O'Dea, not seeing eye to eye with the former President Donald Trump there. Again, trying to make the case that Colorado should elect a moderate Democrat. As soon as we have numbers, we'll bring them to you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE: WISCONSIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANDELA BARNES; RON JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Senate race in Wisconsin also pivotal tonight. Mandela Barnes, a lieutenant governor, challenging the Republican Senator Ron Johnson, seeking a third term, waiting for numbers coming in there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR: WISCONSIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TONY EVERS; TIM MICHELS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Wisconsin governor race. Governor Tony Evers