 so there's really something for everybody there. And I know a lot of (inaudible) stylists have been on a lot of shoots, this is what everybody's using...\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is the one they use?\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...this is from \uc2 Wacoal\uc2 . It is the one to get.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The other staple everybody needs is a really good sports bra.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right. And if you've been at a gym or outside seeing people running this is the sports bra everybody...\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is the one, mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LULULEMON ENERGY LONGLINE BRA\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...is wearing. This is the Lululemon Energy Bra. We spoke to \uc2 Google\uc2  and they gave us data that the most searched term for sports bras right now is a sports bra with support...\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ah, yes.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...you're not going to do better than this. Energy (inaudible) has over 1700 positive reviews. People love it because is it has no friction so you can work out and feel really comfortable. It comes in sizes 2 to 14, B to D cup.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you get a lot of coverage in this, which is nice for working out.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly, exactly.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this is something, you know, backless, strapless, lower back...\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...it's always impossible. What do you do with these?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FASHION FORMS SEAMLESS BACKLESS ADHESIVE BRA\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, listen. These, this is the Fashion Forms from Nordstrom. The search from \uc2 Google\uc2 , people have been searching for backless bras, it has doubled in this past year because so many designers are doing backless and cutouts. I don't know who asked for all these cutouts. They're driving me crazy, but at least we have the Fashion Form's Adhesive Bra from Nordstrom. What people love about this one is it's not disposable...\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...sometimes you get those and then you wear them once and you throw them out. This has a durable adhesive you can use, wear it up to many hours...\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You just kind of wipe it down, right?\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...you wipe it down then it will re-stick. So it's great to wear, you know, for wedding season, the holidays are coming up. This is the perfect thing for you.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're saving a lot of ladies out there, Lori. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Everybody, we've got an exclusive digital discount on one of the bras that you saw here this morning, so you got to scan that qr code or go to our website, goodmorningamerica.com to claim that discount while supplies last. Coming up, two words, Gio, salsa. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Can't wait.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221026eia700069\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE LATEST BREAST CANCER RESEARCH NEW ADVANCES IN TREATMENT, DIAGNOSIS, PREVENTION\b0\par\par\uc2 1,522 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN'S NUCLEAR WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIANS IN RETREAT\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NUCLEAR, PUTIN, WARNING, CUBAN MISSILE\par \par \uc2 RUSSIANS, FLEE, DRAFT, UKRAINE, WAR CRIMES\par \par \uc2 VEGAS, STABBINGS, INJURIES, KOREN\par \par \uc2 DOJ, TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, "NYT", CLASSIFIED\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT, ECONOMY, INFLATION, WALL STREET, FED\par \par \uc2 SINGH, SALGADO, KIDNAPPING, MURDER, EMPLOYEE\par \par \uc2 EBOLA, SCREENING, AIRPORTS, REROUTING\par \par \uc2 IAN, SEARCH, RESCUES, STRUCTURES, INSURANCE\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS, WILD CARD, JUDGE, PUJOLS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CHARGES, FEDS, TAXES, "WASHINGTON POST"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, UTILITIES, BANKS, ZELLE, VICTIMS, PLANOS\par \par \uc2 "DAHMER", NETFLIX, MURPHY, RUSHFIELD, ISBELL, MAIRNAZ\par \par \uc2 LIAM, CHEERLEADERS, POM-POMS, ROUTINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROPICAL DEPRESSION 13\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT: NEW NUCLEAR WARNING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, PUTIN, NUCLEAR, WARNING, ARMAGEDDON\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT, ECONOMY, INFLATION, RECESSION\par \par \uc2 BULLY, CULTURE, KIDS, SIMMONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 INFLAMMATORY BREAST CANCER, NOLEN, ARNOLD\par \par \uc2 EMBED, CAMPAIGN TRAIL, GEORGIA\par \par \uc2 BRA, NO-WIRE, STRAPLESS, SPORTS BRA, BACKLESS, ADHESIVE\par \par \uc2 SALSA, DANCING, LESSON, SOSA, BAILA SOCIETY\par \par \uc2 FUNK, BREAST CANCER, RESEARCH, TREATMENT, PREVENTION\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "Gma," everybody. Of course, it's Breast Cancer Awareness Month and there are some new advancements in the fight against the disease. We have breast cancer surgeon Doctor Kristi Funk, friend of our show around here, and co-founder of Pink Lotus. She joins us now to walk us through some of the latest research, and we're talking first, Doctor Funk, about the new indications for a drug to treat the disease.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENHERTU IS A DRUG NOW ABLE TO BE USED FOR SOME PEOPLE WITH HER2-LOW BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 That's right. Enhertu, it is a game changer for all the metastatic HER2-lows out there. So, HER2 positive cancers have a ton of receptors on the surface, 80 percent of cancers don't have, they're HER2 negative, but if you look closer, some of them have a few receptors. These are you HER2-lows and they area annihilated by the drug Enhertu, which is an antibody associated with a chemo and like a missile, that antibody hits the cancer cell, which then is tricked into letting it inside it, doesn't know the chemo is there to kill, which it effectively does...\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 ...and then the marble gets released, or the chemo, and it can literally just roll on over to the cancer cell next door...\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow. Fascinating.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 ...and kill it. So, it is increasing survival rates. If you're HER2 negative, ask your doctor if you are not in fact HER2-low. It's a new subcategory.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's, we were wondering how that was going to work. That, that, you sold us.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 It works well. Yes. Kinetic sand.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we've got another one here that's talking about how, changes in how to diagnose breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 We are making huge strides in precision medicine, so if you've ever had a solid tumor cancer, so lung, liver, prostate, breast, this test can help you monitor for recurrence early. If you have active disease it can let you know if the therapy is working or not, or if you have a big decision like, you know, I already got rid of the cancer with surgery do I really need the chemotherapy? Signatera can give you answers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIGNATERA IS NEWER TEST TO HELP WITH DISEASE SURVEILLANCE DURING AND AFTER TREATMENT\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 Your doctor has to order it or go to tumordna.com to order it yourself. But, what it is is a blood test made out of 16 different DNA mutations that belong to your cancer. So then they come to your house and draw your blood. This completely goes through insurance. They run the blood through this custom built test. If you're truly cured you should never have any of these Legos lurking in your bloodstream, right, so we check you every three months for two years. If you're still negative there's less than three percent chance you will recur. But if it turns positive, this happens nine and a half months before a PET CT lights up or tumor markers rise up, so you have a chance to intervene and hopefully stave off the impending recurrence. Tumordna.com.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow. All right, Doctor, that is incredible. Let's turn to what so many people often talk about, diet. How can that have an impact and specifically sugar and carbs here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: A WHOLE FOOD PLANT-BASED DIET IS LINKED TO A LOWER RISK OF ALL-CAUSE MORTALITY FOR BREAST CANCER PATIENTS\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 Right. So, sugar does fuel cancer, but it also fuels every single cell in your body so should we avoid them? A large study of 8900 nurses with breast cancer looked at their carb intake and their mortality risk, so what did they find? Those who had the highest consumption of added sugar, so you adding a little bit of sugar to your coffee or the food industry adding a little high fructose corn syrup to your ketchup or your yogurt, these people had the highest mortality of all. But you take that fructose and put it back in its original grape package, no fruit had an elevation in mortality.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 You take the fruit and divorce it from its fiber and put it into juice form, these are your second highest mortality groups...\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 ...the juice consumers. Similarly, if you keep the whole grain, so whole wheat bread, whole oats, these people had no increase in mortality. You divorce the bran and the germ and you grind it into white rice and instant oats, instantly your blood sugar rises, your insulin rises and your mortality goes up.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 The one and only group that actually had a drop in mortality for high consumption was the vegetable consuming group, which is why I always say eat plants, crush cancer.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's amazing.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 There is one more magical food, though...\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. Tell us about this.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 ...that I want to tell you about.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is the one I've been very curious about...\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 Okay. So, it is not a...\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...mushrooms and a study associated with it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGHER MUSHROOM CONSUMPTION IS ASSOCIATED WITH AN OVER 30 PERCENT LOWER RISK OF BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 Right, it's not a fruit or a vegetable, it's a fungus, so the study showed that high versus low mushroom consumers had 30 percent less breast cancer, so shroom it up.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Shroom it up.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What is high consumption of, what would that be considered a high consumption of (inaudible) ?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 A serving a day, literally, one study showed that a half a white button mushroom a day decreased breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 So, just small amounts.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. Got one more over here.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, you know, we can't ever forget here. You know, it helps to have a support group.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUDDY UP! A HELPING HAND CAN HELP IMPROVE CANCER OUTCOMES\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 Indeed it does. So, studies show that those who have higher levels of psychosocial support, indeed, have less mortality from breast cancer. Who doesn't want longevity and friends, so, I encourage everyone to go to pinklotus.com and look for your local chapter. There are 25 throughout the country where we come together to hike, bike, cook, and kick cancer, or find your breast buddy where thrivers come together for support and friendship.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Doctor Funk...\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Amazing.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...this is incredible. Thank you so much for sharing. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks for being here.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR KRISTI FUNK (BREAST CANCER SURGEON)\par \par \uc2 Thanks.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, folks. We want to turn now to Danielle Breezy from our Nashville station, WKRN.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221026eia70006c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN'S NUCLEAR WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIANS IN RETREAT\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NUCLEAR, PUTIN, WARNING, CUBAN MISSILE\par \par \uc2 RUSSIANS, FLEE, DRAFT, UKRAINE, WAR CRIMES\par \par \uc2 VEGAS, STABBINGS, INJURIES, KOREN\par \par \uc2 DOJ, TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, "NYT", CLASSIFIED\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT, ECONOMY, INFLATION, WALL STREET, FED\par \par \uc2 SINGH, SALGADO, KIDNAPPING, MURDER, EMPLOYEE\par \par \uc2 EBOLA, SCREENING, AIRPORTS, REROUTING\par \par \uc2 IAN, SEARCH, RESCUES, STRUCTURES, INSURANCE\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS, WILD CARD, JUDGE, PUJOLS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CHARGES, FEDS, TAXES, "WASHINGTON POST"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, UTILITIES, BANKS, ZELLE, VICTIMS, PLANOS\par \par \uc2 "DAHMER", NETFLIX, MURPHY, RUSHFIELD, ISBELL, MAIRNAZ\par \par \uc2 LIAM, CHEERLEADERS, POM-POMS, ROUTINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROPICAL DEPRESSION 13\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT: NEW NUCLEAR WARNING\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM. Breaking overnight, President Biden sounds the alarm on the growing nuclear threat, saying it's the highest since the Cuban missile crisis with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's military losing ground in Ukraine, troops retreating. This, as Russians are fleeing Putin's military draft. Two men even sailed to Alaska, now asking the US for asylum.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THIS MORNING: ALL EYES ON JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All eyes on the new jobs report. What it could tell us about inflation and a possible recession.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TACKLING BULLYING: HOW TO HELP YOUR CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Breaking down bully culture. The surprising new numbers about just how common bullying is for kids. How your behavior as a parent could be impacting them and what to do if you think your child is the bully.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK: INFLAMMATORY BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Shining a spotlight on inflammatory breast cancer, a little known and aggressive form of the disease. One mom shares her experience beating it and the group that helped her and other women navigate the diagnosis. Plus, renowned breast cancer surgeon, Doctor Kristi Funk is here with the latest advances in battling the disease.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISPANIC HERITAGE MONTH: TEACHING SALSA\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're celebrating Hispanic heritage month, embracing the art of the dance.\par \par \uc2 EZRA SOSA (DANCE PRO)\par \par \uc2 Are you ready to salsa?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Vamos.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Gio Benitez getting his first ever salsa lesson.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 This is a workout.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE: "FUNNY GIRL"\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And it's nothing but sunshine in Times Square. Lea Michele is here live taking on Barbra Streisand's famous "Funny Girl" role. She and the cast are bringing us a special performance and she's saying...\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE ("FUNNY GIRL")\par \par \uc2 Hello, gorgeous. Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, Lea Michele. And, boy, she is getting rave reviews for that. We cannot wait for the performance. Hope you all are doing well this morning.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes, everyone. It's going to be right out there in Times Square. And something else we want to share with you, do you remember when we first came, started the show, what George said to me?\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, I do.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 George said to me, a comment about what I was wearing.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 T.J., you have a new outfit every single day.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It was a compliment, not just a comment.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It was a great compliment, but you always talk to me about how diverse my attire is, but I conducted an experiment this morning.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How vast it is actually.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 No, how vast. But, I conducted an experiment this week that you were a part of and didn't know. Put this up on screen. Everyone, George, I have worn the same blue suit every day this week.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, like the Australian guy.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And, and you didn't notice a thing. To your point, nobody's ever going to notice, and I've been sitting next to you all week in this same suit.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Well, I'm glad to see you're a little more thrifty than I expected.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes. Thank you, George. It was for you. Same suit all week, but to your point, I should get rid of a lot of suits.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Only a man could get away with wearing the same thing, I would like to note, every day and no one notice (inaudible), but I'm not bitter. This morning, we've got a new weekly series to tell you about, it's called "The Right Stuff." We've been telling you about it. This one is going to help you find the best buys this week. Lori is bringing us the best bras as we recognize breast cancer awareness month. So, we'll tell you all about that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221026eia700062\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FIGHTING INFLAMMATORY BREAST CANCER WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT THIS FORM OF THE DISEASE\b0\par\par\uc2 994 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN'S NUCLEAR WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIANS IN RETREAT\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NUCLEAR, PUTIN, WARNING, CUBAN MISSILE\par \par \uc2 RUSSIANS, FLEE, DRAFT, UKRAINE, WAR CRIMES\par \par \uc2 VEGAS, STABBINGS, INJURIES, KOREN\par \par \uc2 DOJ, TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, "NYT", CLASSIFIED\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT, ECONOMY, INFLATION, WALL STREET, FED\par \par \uc2 SINGH, SALGADO, KIDNAPPING, MURDER, EMPLOYEE\par \par \uc2 EBOLA, SCREENING, AIRPORTS, REROUTING\par \par \uc2 IAN, SEARCH, RESCUES, STRUCTURES, INSURANCE\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS, WILD CARD, JUDGE, PUJOLS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CHARGES, FEDS, TAXES, "WASHINGTON POST"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, UTILITIES, BANKS, ZELLE, VICTIMS, PLANOS\par \par \uc2 "DAHMER", NETFLIX, MURPHY, RUSHFIELD, ISBELL, MAIRNAZ\par \par \uc2 LIAM, CHEERLEADERS, POM-POMS, ROUTINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROPICAL DEPRESSION 13\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT: NEW NUCLEAR WARNING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, PUTIN, NUCLEAR, WARNING, ARMAGEDDON\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT, ECONOMY, INFLATION, RECESSION\par \par \uc2 BULLY, CULTURE, KIDS, SIMMONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 INFLAMMATORY BREAST CANCER, NOLEN, ARNOLD\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, George. We want to turn now to our breast cancer awareness series "Thriving in Pink." And, this morning we are highlighting an aggressive form of the disease that can be difficult to diagnose.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it is known as inflammatory breast cancer. And Deb Roberts is here with what to know about all of this. Good morning, Deb.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Cecilia. Yeah, we need to pay attention to this one, women and the men who love them. We've heard those emotional stories about a woman finding a lump in her breast or a mammogram detecting it and a cancer diagnosis following. That is often caught early and a woman's life is spared. Well, there's another kind of breast cancer that you probably have never heard of and that typically goes undetected until it's hard to treat. But a top researcher is now sounding the alarm in hopes of saving more lives.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In January of 2013, Katrece Nolen was on top of the world. Then a 37-year-old busy mom of three and engineer, she'd recently launched her own consulting company.\par \par \uc2 KATRECE NOLEN (DIAGNOSED WITH IBC)\par \par \uc2 It was a great time, figuring out how to make this business happen and juggling life as a mom and as a wife.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But one day, while playing with her son, Katrece noticed her left breast was swollen.\par \par \uc2 KATRECE NOLEN (DIAGNOSED WITH IBC)\par \par \uc2 By that night, there was definitely a noticeable change in the size of my left breast.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She says her doctor suspected an infection, so Katrece began antibiotics and also got a mammogram. The results were inconclusive and the swelling continued. Then came a devastating diagnosis, inflammatory breast cancer, or IBC.\par \par \uc2 KATRECE NOLEN (DIAGNOSED WITH IBC)\par \par \uc2 My first thought was, you know, well, what is going to happen with my kids if I'm not here?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLING INFLAMMATORY BREAST CANCER. ONE MOTHER'S BATTLE AGAINST THIS RARE AND AGGRESSIVE FORM OF THE DISEASE\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Katrece soon got more difficult news. Ibc accounts for only about one percent to five percent of all breast cancers in the US and the overall five-year survival rate is estimated at 40 percent, but that depends on the stage and the person's health. Ibc also tends to occur more frequently in black women under 40 and may be difficult to spot on a mammogram.\par \par \uc2 DR NAOTO UENO (BREAST ONCOLOGIST UNIV OF TEXAS MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 Inflammatory breast cancer basically presents with redness of the breast and it's swollen actually. There's four stages in breast cancer, so ibc diagnosis automatically categorized as three. One-third will have stage four, so it is fairly advanced at the time of the diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is truly an aggressive cancer.\par \par \uc2 DR NAOTO UENO (BREAST ONCOLOGIST UNIV OF TEXAS MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 Yes, but we could do something about it. You just have to work with the right specialist and there's always a great chance to help.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That help often starts with this woman, Terry Arnold, who created the ibc Network Foundation 11 years ago after she says experienced months of missed diagnoses.\par \par \uc2 TERRY ARNOLD (FOUNDER THE IBC NETWORK FOUNDATION)\par \par \uc2 I wanted to network with other women to learn because there was this void.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Terry's mission to help fund IBC research and give more women support and resources.\par \par \uc2 TERRY ARNOLD (FOUNDER THE IBC NETWORK FOUNDATION)\par \par \uc2 We need to share our stories. We also need to encourage proper treatment, diagnosis tools so it isn't such a scary thing and we can have more successes.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Katrece says she turned to the ibc Network Foundation to help her understand her treatment plan and in March of 2013 began chemotherapy, followed by a mastectomy and 33 rounds of radiation.\par \par \uc2 KATRECE NOLEN (DIAGNOSED WITH IBC)\par \par \uc2 It was the group that helped me to navigate this and essentially helped save my life.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now nearly ten years and no signs of cancer, Katrece is savoring precious moments with the family she'd always dreamed of.\par \par \uc2 KATRECE NOLEN (DIAGNOSED WITH IBC)\par \par \uc2 It is a disease that is survivable, but when you notice a change in your breasts, you cannot deny that change. You have to go seek help.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is such important advice. And some doctors don't even recognize the early signs of ibc, so it is vital for women to advocate for themselves. Katrece says she considers her medical team a team, but she's the captain. She says she demanded accountability and fast action, which very well may have saved her life. Guys.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love that. You're the captain of that team. That's really great advice. Deb, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221026eia700066\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  UNDER FIRE REPORT: WOMAN CLAIMS SENATE CANDIDATE URGED 2ND ABORTION\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NUCLEAR THREAT, RUSSIA, BIDEN, ZELENSKYY, WAR\par \par \uc2 ADAMS, IMMIGRATION, HUMANITARIAN CRISIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW YORK CITY "STATE OF EMERGENCY"\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the breaking news involving former football star, Republican Georgia Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  who, as a candidate, opposes abortion, with no exceptions. Tonight, what "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " is now reporting involving the woman claiming he paid for her abortion. "The Times" now reporting he encouraged her to get a second abortion, too, but she says she refused. Here's ABC's Steve Osunsami, tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: WOMAN CLAIMS SENATE CANDIDATE URGED 2ND ABORTION\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He's the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  hopeful in Georgia and college football legend who has publicly come out against all abortions, no matter a woman's reason. But late this evening, yet another report says that \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  doesn't do as he says. "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " is reporting that the former girlfriend, whose abortion he allegedly paid for in 2009, is now saying he wanted her to have another abortion when she was pregnant with his child two years later. That child is now 10 years old. And "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " says the mother told them that the candidate has very little to do with the child's life outside of court-ordered child support and occasional gifts.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXCERPT FROM "NEW YORK TIMES ARTICLE"\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "He has to be held responsible, just like the rest of us," she told "The Times." "And if you're going to run for office, you need to own your life." Walker is denying that he ever paid for the woman to have an abortion.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 This here, the abortion thing, is false. It's a lie.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But his son, a conservative social media figure, came out against his dad.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIAN WALKER (SON OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Don't lie about your life. You don't get to pretend you're some moral family guy. You don't get to pretend all these things. Do not lie.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This mother literally has the receipts, and has been sharing them with reporters. This is, of course, a Senate seat that could decide which party controls the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 . Many Republicans are standing by \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  tonight. He has made no comments, this evening, about these latest allegations. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All eyes on Georgia, yet again, as the midterms approach. Steve Osunsami. Thank you, Steve.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020221010eia700004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CUTTING EDGE BREAST CANCER RESEARCH HOW IT'S RADICALLY CHANGING THE WAY WE TREAT THE DISEASE\b0\par\par\uc2 903 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES, DE HAAN, \uc2 OPEC\uc2 , OIL\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAS PRICES SURGING IN CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S BEHIND THE LATEST SPIKE TO NEAR RECORD LEVEL?\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES, RUSSIA, \uc2 OPEC\uc2 , OIL\par \par \uc2 THAILAND, DAY CARE, SHOOTING, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 MISSILE TEST, NORTH KOREA, SOUTH KOREA\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DESANTIS, SEARCH, RESCUE, SESSIONS\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION, BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REPORT ON HERSCHEL WALKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN WHO CLAIMS SHE HAD ABORTION SAYS SHE'S MOTHER OF ONE OF HIS CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 JUDGE, BASEBALL, OFFER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "WAYNE'S WORLD"\par \par \uc2 "RUST", SETTLEMENT, BALDWIN, HUTCHINS\par \par \uc2 CHHEDA, SHA, WIETE, PROBE, ARREST, SAR, MURDER, PURDUE\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, DEALS, BERG, AIRFARES, KEYES\par \par \uc2 VOGT, HOME RUN, RETIREMENT, OAKLAND A'S\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS, 8:38\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING FALLOUT: NEW PAIN AT THE PUMP?\par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES, \uc2 OPEC\uc2 , OIL PRODUCTION\par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES\par \par \uc2 MISSING, FAMILY, KIDNAPPING, DHERI, WARNKE\par \par \uc2 JUDD, LOSS, MUSIC, REFLECTING, HELLIGAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 DIAGNOSIS, ABORTION, DAVIS, COLE, BONAPARTIS\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, RESEARCH, JONES, PREJEAN\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Robin. We want to turn now to our breast cancer awareness month series, "Thriving in Pink." Thanks to cutting edge advances there are now better treatments and tests that can determine the best way to tackle the disease. And our Erielle Reshef is here now with that. Good morning and good news.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Great news. These are making such a difference, T.J. And some of those advancements have been made in the effort to fight some of the most aggressive forms of breast cancer, especially in young women. And these new treatments are saving lives.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Cutting-edge research radically changing the way we treat breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA TREVINO JONES (UTHEALTH HOUSTON/MEMORIAL HERMANN CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 There's so many things happening at breakneck speed for cancer and cancer treatment and it's just about time that we finally did that for triple negative breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Around 15 percent of early breast cancers are triple negative, a type of cancer more common in black women under age 40. Domonique Valentine (PH) was diagnosed at age 27.\par \par \uc2 DOMONIQUE VALENTINE (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 My biggest worry, it wasn't losing my hair, it wasn't how I was going to look, it was just surviving. I wanted to live.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Triple negative is more aggressive and had fewer treatment options until now.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA TREVINO JONES (UTHEALTH HOUSTON/MEMORIAL HERMANN CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 We're seeing cancers go away.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Doctors can eliminate tumors before surgery by harnessing the body's own immune system. New research finds the addition of immunotherapy called Keytruda to chemo resulted in better response in these patients before surgery, changing treatment guidelines.\par \par \uc2 YOLA PREJEAN (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Chemo was nothing I was looking forward to.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CUTTING EDGE TECH TO TREAT BREAST CANCER. BREAKTHROUGH ALLOWING SOME WOMEN TO SKIP CHEMO ENTIRELY\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Another breakthrough has allowed women like Yola Prejean to skip chemo entirely. When the Texas native was diagnosed with early stage estrogen-positive breast cancer last year, she worried the side effects of chemo would take her out of the game.\par \par \uc2 YOLA PREJEAN (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I don't have time for this cancer stuff, you know. I said, my grandson plays football. I've got to get to that football game.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Luckily, because Yola's cancer was detected early, she was a candidate for a test called onco-type DX, which used genetic analysis to predict that chemotherapy wouldn't help her beat cancer.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA TREVINO JONES (UTHEALTH HOUSTON/MEMORIAL HERMANN CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 We saw that estrogen was the main driving force for what caused her cancer to grow. Because of that, we were able to avoid chemotherapy and start hormonal therapy.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The tests newly released long-term data suggests that for around 80 percent of patients, the no chemo route works, cancers don't return. This also helps in post-menopausal women whose estrogen-positive breast cancer has spread that their lymph nodes.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA TREVINO JONES (UTHEALTH HOUSTON/MEMORIAL HERMANN CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 What we're learning now is that when estrogen is the driving force, even though a cancer may go to the lymph node, it still may just be estrogen that's driving that and she may not benefit from chemotherapy.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I'm glad to report that both Domonique and Yola are cancer-free now. There are also early studies that show that some pre-cancers can be treated with immunotherapy. It's part of a growing effort to enable the body's own immune system to recognize and attack certain conditions before they become cancer. So, this has been applied to multiple myeloma so far, but can you imagine the impact if it's applied to breast cancer?\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Constant updates that we're getting, and positive news about treatments. Thank you so much for that, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A reason to hope. Sure.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we want to turn to Ginger now. Hey there.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221026eia60000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW REPORT ON HERSCHEL WALKER WOMAN SAYS SHE'S MOTHER OF ONE OF HIS CHILDREN\b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES, DE HAAN, \uc2 OPEC\uc2 , OIL\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAS PRICES SURGING IN CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S BEHIND THE LATEST SPIKE TO NEAR RECORD LEVEL?\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES, RUSSIA, \uc2 OPEC\uc2 , OIL\par \par \uc2 THAILAND, DAY CARE, SHOOTING, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 MISSILE TEST, NORTH KOREA, SOUTH KOREA\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DESANTIS, SEARCH, RESCUE, SESSIONS\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION, BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REPORT ON \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN WHO CLAIMS SHE HAD ABORTION SAYS SHE'S MOTHER OF ONE OF HIS CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to get the latest now on Georgia Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  after he denied paying for an ex-girlfriend's abortion and claims he doesn't know who the woman could be.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "The Daily Beast" is now reporting that the woman is also the mother of one of Walker's children. Rachel Scott is tracking it all. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George, good morning. \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is adamant about this. He calls those allegations a flat out lie, but it's his latest denial that's prompting a new shake-up.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 Let me hear, \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 . Come on.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a new twist in the controversy surrounding Georgia's Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 . "The Daily Beast" reporting the woman he allegedly urged to have an abortion is the mother of one of his children. The anonymous woman told the reporter that Walker, a conservative who opposes abortion, paid for the procedure and even sent a get-well card, something he adamantly denies.\par \par \uc2 NEWS ANCHOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Have you figured out who it is?\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 Not at all. And that's what I hope everyone can see. It's sort of like everyone is anonymous or everyone is leaking and they want you to confess to something you have no clue about.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "The Daily Beast" says, after Walker made those comments, the woman wanted to share more information about her identity, telling the reporter, "I've been civil thus far. I keep my mouth shut, but I'm also not going to get run over time and time again." ABC News has not independently verified the report. The former \uc2 NFL\uc2  player, a vocal critic of absent fathers, admitted in June he had three other children he never talked about publicly.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 You know, I never denied any of my kids and I love them more than I love anything.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Walker has not held any public campaign events this week. Several Republican voters leaving his fundraiser told us they're standing by him.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) With abortion being your top issue and now you have these allegations against the candidate that you are supporting...\par \par \uc2 VOTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I don't believe (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...saying that he paid for an abortion. You don't believe any of it?\par \par \uc2 VOTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Nope.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And as for Walker, he released a statement saying that there's no truth to this report. Of course, the stakes are so high here, this is a race, George, as you know, that could determine which party controls the Senate.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It sure is. Okay, Rachel, thanks very much. Right. T.J.?\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221026eia600009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POST ROE V WADE AMERICA ONE WOMAN'S STRUGGLE TO GET AN ABORTION AFTER DIAGNOSIS\b0\par\par\uc2 832 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES, DE HAAN, \uc2 OPEC\uc2 , OIL\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAS PRICES SURGING IN CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S BEHIND THE LATEST SPIKE TO NEAR RECORD LEVEL?\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES, RUSSIA, \uc2 OPEC\uc2 , OIL\par \par \uc2 THAILAND, DAY CARE, SHOOTING, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 MISSILE TEST, NORTH KOREA, SOUTH KOREA\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DESANTIS, SEARCH, RESCUE, SESSIONS\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION, BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REPORT ON HERSCHEL WALKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN WHO CLAIMS SHE HAD ABORTION SAYS SHE'S MOTHER OF ONE OF HIS CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 JUDGE, BASEBALL, OFFER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "WAYNE'S WORLD"\par \par \uc2 "RUST", SETTLEMENT, BALDWIN, HUTCHINS\par \par \uc2 CHHEDA, SHA, WIETE, PROBE, ARREST, SAR, MURDER, PURDUE\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, DEALS, BERG, AIRFARES, KEYES\par \par \uc2 VOGT, HOME RUN, RETIREMENT, OAKLAND A'S\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS, 8:38\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING FALLOUT: NEW PAIN AT THE PUMP?\par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES, \uc2 OPEC\uc2 , OIL PRODUCTION\par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES\par \par \uc2 MISSING, FAMILY, KIDNAPPING, DHERI, WARNKE\par \par \uc2 JUDD, LOSS, MUSIC, REFLECTING, HELLIGAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 DIAGNOSIS, ABORTION, DAVIS, COLE, BONAPARTIS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to "Impact," the new weekly series by "Nightline" that dives into current issues by focusing on the people at the center of them. The first episode looks at post-Roe versus Wade America. Rachel Scott is back. She spoke to families with a range of different perspectives. Good morning, again, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin. Good morning to you. Yeah, these are raw and emotional conversations. Our team decided to travel the country to explore all angles of this divisive issue and see the impact just 100 days after Roe versus Wade was overturned.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (PARENT AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 It's heartbreaking. The agony, the pain, the confusion from all of this.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When Nancy Davis found out she was pregnant this summer it never occurred to her she would be sitting down to tell this story.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (PARENT AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We were elated.\par \par \uc2 SHEDRIC COLE (PARENT AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 This was a planned pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "THIS WAS A PLANNED PREGNANCY." LOUISIANA WOMAN DENIED ABORTION AFTER FATAL DIAGNOSIS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just weeks earlier, the Supreme Court handed down the Dobbs decision, overturning Roe v. Wade. Nancy and her fiance, Shedric weren't thinking about abortion until they suddenly learned their fetus had a deadly diagnosis, a crania.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (PARENT AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 Imagine being told that your baby, some of his brain is missing. It's heartbreaking. It's devastating.\par \par \uc2 SHEDRIC COLE (PARENT AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We had to come to terms with the fact that these babies just don't survive.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (PARENT AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I was carrying my baby to bury my baby. That was the worst day of my life. The doctors advised us that we should terminate, but whenever it came down for us to get the procedure, we were denied.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The decision in Dobbs versus Jackson Women's Health essentially gave each state the power to control access to abortion. Louisiana was one of the states to immediately ban it. But there were exceptions, a crania is not one of them.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (PARENT AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We contacted a few different doctors in Louisiana. No one was doing the abortions, absolutely nobody. To process the information about your baby is one thing, but to add navigating through the system, through the laws, through the different states, that's a whole other animal. It was very difficult.\par \par \uc2 SHEDRIC COLE (PARENT AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 Chaotic.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The issue deeply personal for women across the country. Others like Teresa Bonopartis in New York see the fall of Roe as a step in the right direction. She had an abortion as a teenager and now regrets it.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There are women that feel like they cannot go through with their pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 TERESA BONOPARTIS (DIRECTOR LUMINA)\par \par \uc2 We've told women that they're not capable of doing this and they are capable of doing it if they have the right help.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Teresa works with Good Counsel Homes, a non-profit that offers resources to expecting mothers, and a program for women who regret their abortions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN SHARES HER STORY OF REGRET OVER GETTING AN ABORTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good Counsel Homes offers job training and free housing for new and expecting mothers. As for Nancy Davis, she did end up getting an abortion, but she had to travel from Louisiana to New York for the appointment. And her story is now the new reality for so many women across the country, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, but good that you showed both sides of this issue. Thank you, Rachel. Really appreciate it. And want to let folks know that the premiere of "Impact" by "Nightline" is available now on \uc2 Hulu\uc2  with new episodes every Thursday. T.J.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221026eia60000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POST-ROE IMPACT EXPLORING THE IMPACT OF THE OVERTURNING OF ROE V. WADE ACROSS AMERICA\b0\par\par\uc2 1,867 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 DAVIS, COLE, PELTEN, MARRA, BONOPARTIS, PLIMPTON, PHILIPPS\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks for joining us. Now, to the national debate over banning abortion. We traveled across the country to see up close how women on both sides of the issue are grappling with the fallout. Some sharing stories about being denied access that are as painful as they are powerful, others describing their profound decisions to have their babies, despite the obstacles. Here's ABC's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hey, Juju. It's been a little over 100 days since the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade, and with the midterms just around the corner, women across the country are starting to feel a sense of urgency. So, we decided to travel state to state to explore all angles of this divisive issue, with real, raw and emotional conversations, exploring the impact in a post-Roe America.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATON ROUGE, LOUISIANA\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (MOTHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 It's heartbreaking. The agony, the pain, the confusion from all of this.\par \par \uc2 SHEDRIC COLE (FATHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We looked at this picture, you know, over and over and over and over again, you know, getting to the point where we stopped looking at it. Because...\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (MOTHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 It's hard to look at it.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When Nancy Davis found out she was pregnant this summer, it never occurred to her she would be sitting down to tell this story.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (MOTHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We were elated.\par \par \uc2 SHEDRIC COLE (FATHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 This was a planned pregnancy. We wanted a fourth child.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (MOTHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I think I may have done a dance.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just weeks earlier, the Supreme Court handed down the Dobbs decision, overturning Roe versus Wade. Nancy and her fianc\u233\'00\'E9 Cedric weren't thinking about abortion until they suddenly learned their fetus had a deadly diagnosis, acrania.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (MOTHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 Imagine being told that your baby, some of his brain is missing and the skull is missing. It's heartbreaking. It's devastating.\par \par \uc2 SHEDRIC COLE (FATHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We had to come to terms with the fact that these babies just don't survive.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (MOTHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I was carrying my baby to bury my baby. That was the worst day of my life. The doctors, they advised us that we should terminate. But whenever it came down for us to get the procedure, we were denied. Women's Hospital was scared of prosecution, and they were scared of being fined.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The decision in Dobbs versus Jackson Women's Health essentially gave each state the power to control access to abortion. Louisiana was one of the states to immediately ban it, but there were exceptions. Acrania is not one of them.\par \par \uc2 NANCY DAVIS (MOTHER AND ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We contacted a few different doctors in Louisiana. No one was going near abortions. Absolutely nobody.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 14 STATES HAVE CEASED ABORTION SERVICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 5 STATES HAVE ABORTION ON THE BALLOT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Louisiana is just one state to ban abortions. And with the midterms just weeks away, at least 14 states have also banned it, while five other states have abortion on the ballot this November. This Saturday marks the fifth anniversary of the women's March to advocate for abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Our bodies, our choice.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, we set out to explore this issue in "Nightline's" new weekly series streaming on \uc2 Hulu\uc2 , "Impact."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMPACT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Our first episode takes a closer look at how the Supreme Court's decision is changing the landscape of women's rights.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA PLIMPTON (ACTOR/ADVOCATE/CO-FOUNDER OF A IS FOR)\par \par \uc2 The first time I had an abortion, I was 19. There was never any question in my mind about what I would do.\par \par \uc2 BUSY PHILIPPS (ACTOR/ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I was 15. Yeah. I was 15. I was just really devastated, and I knew there was no chance in hell that I was having a baby.\par \par \uc2 JAMEELA JAMIL (ACTOR/ACTIVIST/FOUNDER OF I\par \par \uc2 I was 26 when I needed an abortion. It saved my life. It was the best decision I ever made.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We speak to people across the spectrum on the issue.\par \par \uc2 SAVANNAH CRAVEN (INFLUENCER/ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is death. Abortion is evil. It's destructive. It's unnecessary.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANNA PUEBLA (MOTHER/ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I feel that everyone should give their baby a chance, a chance at life, whether you want to parent or not.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And talk about what needs to change as we enter a post-Roe world.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 We won't go back.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The ripple effect is reaching across the country, including traditionally blue states. In Michigan, voters will decide this November if they want to protect abortion in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 I would say student parents are probably the most hidden population, which was where I had a lot of trouble as a student, was no one had really heard of my identity. But statistics show one in five students are student parents.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jessica Pelten is a graduate of \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 . It's precisely places like this that could feel the impact of the Roe reversal. More than a third of women who have abortions every year do so before the age of 25.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Hey, Amber, I'm gonna get your cereal. Let's get your breakfast and get your lunch packed, honey.\par \par \uc2 CHILD (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I like it.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think there's a narrative that young mothers, young fathers can't graduate from college. College isn't even an option. It's out of the question. Do you think that's wrong?\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, because if it wasn't for her, I never would've gone. College was never on my radar, at all. I never felt like I had a reason to go.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Have a good workday.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After her daughter was diagnosed with a brain tumor...\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Let's get in the car.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...that changed.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 After she was diagnosed...\par \par \uc2 CROSSING GUARD (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Good morning. Happy Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 ...she was three, and I asked how she would have a normal life. So, I signed up for college to show her, like, if I can have a normal life while raising her, she can do it, too.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Oh, there's the bell. Have the best day.\par \par \uc2 CHILD (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Let's go.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 I want her to go in college. I want that to be a goal. I want her to see me do it.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2  has more resources than most for student parents. Lactation rooms...\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 I am going to show you guys the study room.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...a dedicated study space, and a pilot program for on-campus daycare. Some of those, thanks to Jessica. She now works at the Center for the Education of Women, known as CEW+, an organization that advocates for students from underserved groups with scholarships and emergency funding. Dr. Tiffany Marra is the program's executive director. Jessica says she's been a critical mentor.\par \par \uc2 DR. TIFFANY MARRA (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR CEW+)\par \par \uc2 The hardest part for me is seeing students who advocate so hard for themselves, knowing that they might not be able to create the change that they want to see in the four years that they're here.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Marra says that with Roe versus Wade overturned, supporting student parents should be a priority at all campuses.\par \par \uc2 DR. TIFFANY MARRA (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR CEW+)\par \par \uc2 I would imagine with the Roe v. Wade Supreme Court decision, that there might be greater demand. It would be a travesty if, because of, of bans that are now getting enacted across states, we lost a population of the higher education system. To me, that would be the worst possible outcome.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You don't really even talk about abortion or politics around this issue at work. Why?\par \par \uc2 JESSICA PELTEN (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 I don't talk about politics as a student or in my personal life or at work, because it causes a lot of divide and ill feelings about each other. I just believe that everyone should be supportive of student parents, regardless of where they feel, politically.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Around the country, there are other programs designed to help expecting mothers. Many are faith-based, like Good Counsel Homes, the nonprofit which provides a place to stay, school and job training for free. Good Counsel also has a program that helps women who regret getting an abortion.\par \par \uc2 THERESA BONOPARTIS (DIRECTOR OF LUMINA\par \par \uc2 My name is Theresa Bonapartis, director of Lumina. It's an outreach for people that are suffering, to let them know that they're not crazy and they're not alone and that there is help. There can be healing from a past abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I want you to tell me a little bit about how this program got started.\par \par \uc2 THERESA BONOPARTIS (DIRECTOR OF LUMINA\par \par \uc2 That would go from my own story. I had an abortion when I was a teenager, and to say that my life, you know, changed after that is an understatement. I hated myself.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Theresa says she's encountered dozens of women who feel guilt and shame after their abortions, and that her program helps them find healing.\par \par \uc2 THERESA BONOPARTIS (DIRECTOR OF LUMINA\par \par \uc2 Nobody wants to hear us, on both sides, sometimes. So, I think that people that have suffered abortion often feel very much stuck in the middle of the debate.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There are women who feel they cannot go through with their pregnancies...\par \par \uc2 THERESA BONOPARTIS (DIRECTOR OF LUMINA\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...that they have to decide to have an abortion, because they're young and they feel it may limit their opportunities.\par \par \uc2 THERESA BONOPARTIS (DIRECTOR OF LUMINA\par \par \uc2 But don't you think that we're the ones that have put that in their heads? We've told women that they're not capable of doing this, and they are capable of doing it, if they have the right help.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC NEWS IMPACT BY NIGHTLINE: ORIGINAL SERIES THURSDAYS ONLY ON HULU\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And "IMPACT x Nightline" is now streaming on \uc2 Hulu\uc2 . New episodes drop every Thursday.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT ON\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And up next, one-on-one with Huma Abedin. Moving on from scandal, lies and heartbreak.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020221007eia600002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WALKER DENIES ALLEGATIONS GA SENATE CANDIDATE CALLS ABORTION REPORT "A LIE"\b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, STABBING, DOREN\par \par \uc2 DAY CARE, SHOOTING, THAILAND, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DAY CARE CENTER MASSACRE\par \par \uc2 PARDONS, BIDEN, MARIJUANA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN'S SURPRISE PARDONS\par \par \uc2 ISIS, RAID, SYRIA, NORTH KOREA, MISSILE TEST\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION, BAN, MIDTERM ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALKER DENIES ALLEGATIONS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to Georgia, where \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the Republican Senate candidate, there, took questions today about that report that he paid for an ex-girlfriend's abortion. Now, this has become an issue, because as a candidate, he opposes abortion rights, with no exceptions. ABC's Rachel Scott, on how he answered.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GA SENATE CANDIDATE CALLS ABORTION REPORT "A LIE"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  facing reporters for the first time...\par \par \uc2 SUPPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26since that explosive report he once paid for an ex-girlfriend to get an abortion. As a candidate, Walker opposes abortion rights, without any exceptions.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 I know why you're here. I do. And you're here because the Democrats are desperate to hold onto this seat, here. They're desperate to make this race about my family.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It comes just hours after "The Daily Beast" reported the woman Walker allegedly urged to have an abortion is also the mother of one of his four children. She has chosen to remain anonymous, telling "The Daily Beast," "He didn't accept responsibility for the kid we did have together, and now he isn't accepting responsibility for the one we didn't have." ABC News has not independently confirmed the story. The woman showed "The Daily Beast" a receipt from an abortion clinic and a $700-check she claims is from Walker. She says he gave her this get well card, too. Adding, "He didn't express any regret. He said, 'relax and recover.' He seemed pretty pro-choice to me." Walker insists the story is not true.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 This here, the abortion thing is false. It's a lie.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One person who clearly doesn't believe him, his own son from his first marriage.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIAN WALKER (SON OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Don't lie about your life. You don't get to pretend you're some moral family guy. You don't get to pretend all these things. Do not lie.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Your own son has said that you're not a family man. He has called you a liar. Why should Georgia voters believe your words over his?\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 Because I love my son so much. He's a great, little man. I love him to death. And you know what? I will always love him, no matter what my son says.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When asked about that $700-check he allegedly sent the woman to pay for the abortion, Walker said he gives money to people all the time. Republicans are banking on this race to help them win control of the Senate in November, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott with us, again, tonight. Rachel, thank you. And we should note that Rachel will have much more later tonight on the issue of abortion in America, part of a new program, "IMPACT x Nightline" on Hulu.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "IMPACT X NIGHTLINE"\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Rachel and the team reporting on this key issue, viewpoints from all sides. Again, "IMPACT x Nightline" on Hulu.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020221007eia600006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WOMEN AND BURNOUT! AMOUNT OF HOUSEWORK AFFECTS WOMEN'S MENTAL HEALTH\b0\par\par\uc2 1,120 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CRISIS\par \par \uc2 IAN, CRISIS, SEARCH, DISPLACED, RED CROSS\par \par \uc2 IAN, BIDEN, SURVEY, DAMAGE, DESANTIS\par \par \uc2 UKRAINIANS, RUSSIANS, RETREAT, ADVANCES, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 FENTANYL, RAINBOW, HALLOWEEN, NARCAN\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SERIAL KILLER, VIDEO, MCFADDEN\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, ABDUCTION, AROOHI, SINGH, WARNKE, SALGADO\par \par \uc2 MUSK, TWITTER, PURCHASE\par \par \uc2 JUDGE, HOME RUNS, RECORD, MARIS, \uc2 YANKEES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BRADY, BUNDCHEN, DIVORCE, FOOTBALL, "ELLE", TRIGGS\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION, GOP, CHRISTIAN, GROSSMAN\par \par \uc2 LYNN, MUSIC, TRIBUTES, "COAL MINERS DAUGHTER"\par \par \uc2 GENDER REVEAL, BALLOONS, PINK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE-RAVAGED FLORIDA: GROWING HUMANITARIAN CRISIS\par \par \uc2 HUMANITARIAN CRISIS, FLORIDA, HURRICANE\par \par \uc2 RAINBOW FENTANYL, LEGO, HALLOWEEN, PILLS\par \par \uc2 WATTS, AGEISM, HOLLYWOOD, STIGMA, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 WOMEN, CHORES, HEALTH, KERLEY, CLARK, ESGUERRA, RODSKY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, we have a new report on women and burnout. When it comes to how juggling work, kids, and household chores all impact mental health. In the US, women spend four and a half hours each day taking care of their homes and families. For men, 2.8 hours. Eva is back with more on a story we first saw in "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ." We're talking.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was talking to a lot of people and causing fights yesterday. But, I don't have to tell moms this. Moms are tired, but it's not just exhaustion from being busy. A new study finding trying to keep it all going is taking a major toll on their mental health.\par \par \uc2 TESSA KERLEY (MOM OF TWO)\par \par \uc2 Good morning. I have been up for about an hour and 15 minutes.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For many moms, the workday starts right when they wake up, taking care of kids and home as the day dawns.\par \par \uc2 TESSA KERLEY (MOM OF TWO)\par \par \uc2 My husband has already left for work, so it is me getting two kids out the door.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tessa Kerley is a mom of two. She says when she wakes up in the morning it's just go, go, go before she heads to her job as a full-time teacher.\par \par \uc2 TESSA KERLEY (MOM OF TWO)\par \par \uc2 I'm leaving my house a mess, but it's one of those things that it will just stay that way until I get home.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Katie Clark also has two kids. She says just getting out the door in the morning can be a challenge.\par \par \uc2 KATIE CLARK (MOM OF TWO)\par \par \uc2 Me and my husband have a really good routine down. We both wake up with the kids. Today I'm going to be dropping the boys off at school because my husband has to go into the office, so I'll drop them off at day care and then I have to get on my way and get to work.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Jennifer Esguerra, juggling home and work schedules can be a challenge.\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER ESGUERRA (MOM OF THREE)\par \par \uc2 I was up at 4:00 AM yesterday morning to be on a 5:55 AM flight, and now I'm back at the airport trying to get home to my 6-month old, 3-year-old, 5-year-old and my flight was canceled. Being a working mom isn't easy.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And these moms aren't alone. A recently published article in "The Lancet Public Health" looked at 19 studies with information gathered from over 70,000 people around the world finding several conclusions, including that housework and childcare have a greater mental health impact on women than men.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY ON THE MENTAL HEALTH IMPACT OF HOUSEWORK AND CHILDCARE\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the US, women spend four and a half hours each day taking care of their homes and families versus 2.8 hours for men. Eve Rodsky, best-selling author of "Fair Play," says it's not just about the amount of work women are doing at home, but for some, the type of work.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE TASKS THAT MOST NEGATIVELY AFFECT MOM'S MENTAL HEALTH\par \par \uc2 EVE RODSKY (AUTHOR "FAIR PLAY")\par \par \uc2 Men hold cards that they can do at their own timetable, like mowing the lawn. Whereas, women are the ones still to this day responsible for tasks like meal planning, responsible for grocery shopping, and responsible for things like going to get their children when they're sick if a school calls.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it's the amount of time, that difference, double, that really takes the effect on women. Rodsky speaking with moms during the pandemic creating a list she calls the dirty dozen tasks that most negatively affect mom's mental health. Laundry, groceries, meals, home supplies, tidying up, cleaning, dishes, garbage, discipline, screen time, homework, watching the kids, managing their social interactions. These are things nobody really wants to do, a lot of them.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right?\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You can understand how that would take a mental health toll on moms.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And experts say that the imbalance starts even before your kids are able to start running around.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's a lot of reasons for this, but one of the things that I've heard from a lot of moms is some of this starts when babies are born. You know, experts say it could start with paternity leave if we really want to make a change with all of this because dads are often given no leave, they have to take vacation days, or if they're lucky enough, they might get a few weeks for paternity. That shift in the chores starts then, and then it often doesn't change when mom goes back to work. And let's be clear, a lot of men do want to help, they do help, but the difference in time is still there. Women are doing double the work.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Men, men.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have no defense. Let's not even try.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) George?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, I mean, I offered to do, I offered to do this report for you, so you didn't have to work. I mean, it shouldn't fall on you, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, T.J.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Eva. (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You always find a way, don't you, T.J.? How about some "Pop News" now with Lara. I know, shaking our heads. I know.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia500065\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  UNDER FIRE DENIES ALLEGATIONS HE PAID FOR GIRLFRIEND'S ABORTION\b0\par\par\uc2 936 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CRISIS\par \par \uc2 IAN, CRISIS, SEARCH, DISPLACED, RED CROSS\par \par \uc2 IAN, BIDEN, SURVEY, DAMAGE, DESANTIS\par \par \uc2 UKRAINIANS, RUSSIANS, RETREAT, ADVANCES, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 FENTANYL, RAINBOW, HALLOWEEN, NARCAN\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SERIAL KILLER, VIDEO, MCFADDEN\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, ABDUCTION, AROOHI, SINGH, WARNKE, SALGADO\par \par \uc2 MUSK, TWITTER, PURCHASE\par \par \uc2 JUDGE, HOME RUNS, RECORD, MARIS, \uc2 YANKEES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BRADY, BUNDCHEN, DIVORCE, FOOTBALL, "ELLE", TRIGGS\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION, GOP, CHRISTIAN, GROSSMAN\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Very recently, yes. All right, Robes, thank you so much. We want to turn now to the latest on Georgia Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , who supports an abortion ban. But he's under fire because of a report that he paid for a girlfriend's abortion back in 2009. Republicans though are closing ranks around him, as he denounces the report as a lie. Our congressional reporter Rachel Scott is in Atlanta this morning. Good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA SENATE CANDIDATE DENIES ALLEGATIONS HE PAID GIRLFRIEND'S ABORTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, T.J., good morning. And all this controversy is playing out at a critical time. We are less than five weeks out from an election day. This is a race that could decide which party controls the Senate. And that's exactly why you are seeing so many Republicans stand by \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  moving full steam ahead.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP LEADERS CLOSE RANKS AS GEORGIA SENATE CANDIDATE DENIES ABORTION PAYMENT REPORT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning with his campaign rocked by controversy, Republican leaders are rallying behind \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  after allegations that the staunchly anti-abortion candidate paid for a woman to get an abortion.\par \par \uc2 SEN RICK SCOTT (REP) (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 Herschel's going to win and they're starting to see it.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The former Heisman Trophy winner and \uc2 NFL\uc2  star, denying the allegations, dodging cameras as he held a prayer luncheon in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) His campaign kicked us off the property and moved us all the way across the street.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AN OCTOBER SURPRISE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  FIGHTING BACK AGAINST ALLEGATIONS HE PAID FOR GIRLFRIEND'S ABORTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the final stretch of the mid-terms an October surprise. "The Daily Beast" reporting that a woman who asked the website not to use her name for privacy, claims that when she became pregnant in 2009 by Walker, he urged her to have an abortion. The reporter says she provided a $575 bill from an abortion clinic, and a $700 check she claims was reimbursement for the procedure plus expenses. And this, a get well card she says was signed by Walker.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ABC News has not independently confirmed the report. Walker, who is locked in a very tight race with Georgia's Democratic Senator Raphael Warnock, has made his stance on abortion a cornerstone of his campaign. He has denied the woman's allegations, calling the report a "Flat out lie."\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (GEORGIA SENATE CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 No exception in my mind. I believe in life. I believe in life.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But his son Christian, an outspoken conservative with a large social media following, says his father is a hypocrite.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIAN WALKER (SON OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Family values, people? He has four kids, four different women. Wasn't in the house raising one of them. He was out having sex with other women. Do you care about family values?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He said every member of Walker's family had begged him not to run.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIAN WALKER (SON OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Don't lie about your life. You don't get to pretend you're some moral family guy. You don't get to pretend all these things. Do not lie.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In what appeared to be a response to Christian's statements, Walker wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , "I love my son no matter what." Christian's mother is Cindy Grossman. She spoke with ABC News in 2008, accusing Walker of threatening her life.\par \par \uc2 CINDY GROSSMAN (EX-WIFE OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 We were talking and the next thing I knew he just, he got a gun and he put it to my temple. And there was somebody there that was evil.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Walker did not deny that he threatened his former wife, but claims he had no memory of it. In 2008 he revealed he had been diagnosed with a rare mental illness called dissociative identity disorder, formerly known as multiple personality disorder. That same year Walker sat down with ABC's Bob Woodruff.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (GEORGIA SENATE CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I had it the whole time, I just didn't know what it was.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But this morning, despite all the controversy, Republican leaders backing Walker are moving full steam ahead. The head of the RNC insisting "Walker will deliver a safer and more prosperous Georgia."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So all of this has put abortion right back in the spotlight here in Georgia, and the Democrat in this race, Senator Raphael Warnock, is making it clear that he supports abortion rights. He's telling voters they have a very real choice to make this November, guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING LORETTA LYNN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just weeks away from finding out. Rachel, as always, our thanks to you. Coming up, honoring music legend Loretta Lynn and her remarkable legacy. Come on back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia50005x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER DENIES EXPLOSIVE REPORT SAYS HE DID NOT PAY FOR GIRLFRIEND TO GET AN ABORTION\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, MISSILE TEST, JAPAN\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, UKRAINE, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, SEARCH, STEELMAN, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, INVESTIGATION, DOCUMENTS, CANNON\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, CAPITOL, RIOT, OATH KEEPERS, RHODES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OATH KEEPERS ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROSECUTORS SAY MEN PLANNED "ARMED REBELLION" ON JANUARY 6TH\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, SERIAL KILLER, INVESTIGATION, MURDER\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION, MIDTERM, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERSCHEL WALKER DENIES EXPLOSIVE REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP SENATE CANDIDATE SAYS HE DID NOT PAY FOR GIRLFRIEND TO GET AN ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To politics now and the midterm elections just weeks away. A major shake-up in Georgia's Senate race. Republican candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , who backs abortion ban, is denying a report that he paid for an abortion over a decade ago. Congressional correspondent Rachel Scott has the latest.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 Let me hear \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 . Come on.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, Georgia Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  denying an explosive report by "The Daily Beast," alleging the candidate who opposes abortion not only encouraged his then-girlfriend in 2009 to get an abortion herself, but paid for the procedure. The former \uc2 NFL\uc2  player quickly denied the allegations, tweeting, "This is a flat out lie and I deny this in the strongest possible terms." "The Daily Beast" says the woman, who asked not to be identified for privacy reasons, provided a receipt she said is from the clinic, a get-well card she said was from the Heisman Trophy winner and an image of a check from Walker for $700. Overnight, on Fox News, Walker claimed it was a political attack.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 I never asked anyone to get an abortion. I never paid for an abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He said he sends money to a lot of people.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you know the woman that is making this allegation?\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 No, I have no idea, but it is a flat out lie.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And now, one of Walker's sons blasting his father's decision to run for office. Christian Walker, an outspoken conservative with a large social media following, tweeted, "Every family member of \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  asked him not to run for office." Saying that his father chose to "air out all of his dirty laundry in public while simultaneously lying about it."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this could have big implications, George. This is a race that could determine which party controls the Senate, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. Rachel, I know you're going to be in Georgia this week for us for "Power Trip." Thanks very much. Amy?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN'S SOCCER ABUSE SCANDAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCATHING NEW REPORT FINDS "SYSTEMIC" ABUSE & MISCONDUCT\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, coming up, the new investigation rocking women's soccer, finding that players' reports of sexual misconduct, verbal abuse and emotional abuse by some coaches were ignored for years. That's coming up.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia400030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  UNDER FIRE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,541 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 WU, ABUSE, BOAT, PRODUCER, SUICIDE, ASIAN\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION, SENATE, SON, GROSSMAN\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) With the midterm elections now weeks away, a new allegation about the personal life of Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  has emerged. Now his son, Christian, is using his social media fame to denounce his father. Here's ABC's Rachel Scott, in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Georgia Republican Senate hopeful \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is under fire, yet again.\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF FOX NEWS STORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  RESPONDS TO ABORTION ALLEGATIONS: THIS IS A FLAT-OUT LIE, HANNITY\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (GEORGIA REPUBLICAN SENATORIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I can tell you right now, I never asked anyone to get an abortion. I never paid for an abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The staunchly anti-abortion candidate responding on Fox News to allegations that he paid for an ex-girlfriend's abortion more than a decade ago.\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF FOX NEWS INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (GEORGIA REPUBLICAN SENATORIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 And it's a lie. And I'm gonna continue to fight, you know. I tell you, that's what they want. They want this seat.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Walker vigorously advocates a total ban on abortion, with no exceptions. The former Heisman Trophy winner and \uc2 NFL\uc2  star is in a very tight race with Georgia's incumbent Democratic senator, Raphael Warnock. It's just the latest controversy in what has already been a rocky campaign. Walker, today, shying away from the cameras.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's clear \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 's campaign is trying to keep us at a distance. We tried to attend the luncheon that he is attending, today. Well, his campaign kicked us off the property, moved us all the way across the street. We don't know if we're going to get any closer.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DAILY BEAST HEADLINE: 'PRO-LIFE' \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  PAID FOR GIRLFRIEND'S ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "\u8230\'20\'26A $575 RECEIPT FROM THE ABORTION CLINIC\u8230\'20\'26"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "\u8230\'20\'26BANK DEPOSIT RECEIPT THAT INCLUDED AN IMAGE OF A SIGNED $700 PERSONAL CHECK FROM WALKER."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The allegations, reported by "The Daily Beast," were made by a woman claiming to be Walker's ex-girlfriend. The woman, who asked the website not to use her name, to protect her privacy, provided a $575 receipt from the abortion clinic and a bank deposit receipt that included an image of a signed $700 personal check from Walker, which she claims was to reimburse her for the surgery.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "\u8230\'20\'26DEFAMATORY LIE."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also included, what she says was a signed "Get Well" card from Walker, with the phrase "Pray you are feeling better." ABC News has not spoken with the alleged accuser or confirmed "The Daily Beast's" reporting. In response, Walker says he's planning to sue "The Daily Beast" for this, quote, "defamatory lie."\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF SOCIAL MEDIA POST\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIAN WALKER (SON OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 The abortion part drops yesterday. It's literally his handwriting on the card. Okay, I'm done. Done. Everything has been a lie.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "I KNOW MY MOM AND I WOULD REALLY APPRECIATE IT IF MY FATHER HERSCHEL WALKER STOPPED LYING\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOU'RE NOT A 'FAMILY MAN'\u8230\'20\'26"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "EVERY FAMILY MEMBER OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  ASKED HIM NOT TO RUN FOR OFFICE\u8230\'20\'26"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And now criticism from within his own family. Walker's 23-year-old son Christian, a conservative TikToker who has previously campaigned for his father, now denouncing him on social media, writing, "I know my mom and I would really appreciate if my father, \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , stopped lying. You are not a family man." He added that "Every family member of \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  asked him not to run for office," because of his past.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: I LOVE MY SON NO MATTER WHAT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In what was seemingly a response to Christian's statements, Walker wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , "I love my son, no matter what."\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF SOCIAL MEDIA POST\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIAN WALKER (SON OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 I stayed silent as the atrocities committed against my mom were downplayed. You have no idea what me and my mom have survived.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Christian's mother is Cindy Grossman, who was married to Walker for 19 years, after meeting in college.\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF 2008 INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 CINDY GROSSMAN (EX-WIFE OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 He got a gun, and he put it to my temple.\par \par \uc2 BOB WOODRUFF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Put the gun right to your temple? And what did he say?\par \par \uc2 CINDY GROSSMAN (EX-WIFE OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 "I'm gonna blow your effing brains out."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) My colleague, Bob Woodruff, spoke with her in 2008 about allegations that he had threatened her, allegations that have since resurfaced over the course of the Walker campaign.\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF 2008 INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 CINDY GROSSMAN (EX-WIFE OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 I just must have had the strength of God in me, because I just looked him in the eye, and I said, "Go ahead, pull the trigger. I know where I'm going. Do you know where you're going?"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ABC News also spoke to Walker that year about those allegations. And about his Dissociative Identity Disorder diagnosis, once called Multiple Personality Disorder. It's something he wrote about extensively in his 2008 memoir.\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF 2008 INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (GEORGIA REPUBLICAN SENATORIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I told somebody once, you don't want the Herschel that plays football, you don't want the Herschel that do business babysitting your child. You want a different person. When I'm competing, I'm a totally different person.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Walker did not deny he threatened his former wife, but claimed he had no memory of it.\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF 2008 INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 BOB WOODRUFF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you not remember something like that? Because you think that was another alter? Or do you want to get out of have having to talk about it?\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (GEORGIA REPUBLICAN SENATORIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 No, no, no, no. No, I, I, if I can tell you, I'm talking about everything else. If I can remember, I'll talk about it.\par \par \uc2 BOB WOODRUFF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He says he doesn't remember a lot of details of these.\par \par \uc2 CINDY GROSSMAN (EX-WIFE OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 He may not. But I certainly do.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAP OF IRVING, TEXAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "\u8230\'20\'26TALKED ABOUT HAVING A SHOOT-OUT WITH POLICE\u8230\'20\'26"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Cindy says it wasn't just that one incident, that there were other physical confrontations, including choking and multiple threats with different weapons. In 2001, police were called to their home in Irving, Texas. Officers reported that Walker "talked about having a shootout with police." His gun was subsequently confiscated. Cindy has not responded to ABC News' requests for comment. Walker also told Bob Woodruff in 2008 he had been in therapy for DID, and was doing well.\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF 2008 INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (GEORGIA REPUBLICAN SENATORIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'm totally changed from back then to where I'm at today. A lot of people may have these problems, but they are too ashamed or they're too scared to come out and say something. I'm not ashamed because, guys, I'm human.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "HERSCHEL ADDRESSED THESE ISSUES IN DETAIL WITH BOB WOODRUFF 14 YEARS AGO -- HE EVEN WROTE A BOOK ABOUT IT.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE SAME REPORTERS WHO PRAISED HIM FOR HIS COURAGE ARE NOW TRASHING HIM BECAUSE HE'S A REPUBLICAN.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IT IS SHAMEFUL AND IS WHY GOOD PEOPLE DON'T RUN FOR OFFICE." MALLORY BLOUNT, SPOKESPERSON FOR WALKER CAMPAIGN\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we reached out for comment this year, a spokesperson for the Walker campaign told ABC News, "Herschel addressed these issues in detail with Bob woodruff 14 years ago. He even wrote a book about it. The same reporters who praised him for his courage are now trashing him because he's a Republican. It is shameful, and is why good people don't run for office." The National Republican Senatorial Committee continues to stand by their candidate.\par \par \uc2 TARA SETMAYER (GOP STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 I think that is a terrible reflection on the state of the Republican Party today and politics today, that the tribalism is so strong, that it supersedes character, integrity, honesty, facts. And we're seeing that based off of the continued support for \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  in light of the latest controversy.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While the candidates continue to campaign, some voters may have already made up their minds.\par \par \uc2 TARA SETMAYER (GOP STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 Despite the controversies, despite the accusations of violence, and now the accusation of paying for an abortion after claiming to be pro-life under all circumstances, \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  could still win this race in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Rachel. We'll have an inside and up-to-the-minute look of the state of play in Georgia this Sunday, on "Power Trip," on Hulu.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOME RUN KING\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back, the history made in baseball, tonight.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020221005eia400003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 REMEMBERING LORETTA LYNN LORETTA LYNN, 1932-2022\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP, EMERGENCY APPEAL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALKER DENIES PAYING FOR ABORTION\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EAST COAST FLOOD ALERTS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, SEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHELTERS FILL AS DEATH TOLL RISES\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, SERIAL KILLER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW CASES TIED TO SERIAL KILLINGS\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIANS IN RETREAT\par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, MISSILE TEST, JAPAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: N. KOREA FIRES MISSILE OVER JAPAN\par \par \uc2 LYNN, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING LORETTA LYNN\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, KIDNAPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAMILY OF FOUR KIDNAPPED\par \par \uc2 MUSK, TWITTER, BRADY, BUNDCHEN, DIVORCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 LYNN, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, tonight, here, the Coal Miner's Daughter, in her own words. She was asked how she wanted people to look back on her life, her music. Loretta Lynn, on how she wants to be remembered.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Loretta Lynn was asked how she would you like to be remembered. And she said, as "A good person that never hurt nobody." Then asked if she had any regrets, she said, "No. If I had it to do over, I would go the same route again."\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, we are celebrating a country music legend, tonight. A lot of people playing a little Loretta Lynn, today. I'm David Muir. Thank you for watching. I'll see you right back here, tomorrow night. From all of us here at ABC News, have a good evening. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020221005eia40000c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WALKER DENIES PAYING FOR ABORTION PIVOTAL CASE UPENDED WEEKS BEFORE ELECTION\b0\par\par\uc2 779 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP, EMERGENCY APPEAL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALKER DENIES PAYING FOR ABORTION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And all of this playing out with just 35 days, a little more than a month until the crucial midterm elections. Tonight, the explosive claim involving the former football star, the Republican Senate candidate in Georgia. The report claims \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , who has called for a ban on abortions, no exceptions, that he allegedly paid for a former girlfriend's abortion. What he's now saying, tonight, how he explains the alleged check he gave her, and his own son blasting his father, tonight. Rachel Scott, from Georgia.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PIVOTAL CASE UPENDED WEEKS BEFORE ELECTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The race that could decide control of the Senate...\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 Let me hear, "\uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 ." Come on.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26now upended by the report Georgia's Republican Senate candidate Herschel walker paid for an ex-girlfriend to have an abortion. Walker calls it a flat-out lie. Today, he was ducking reporters at a prayer breakfast in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's clear \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 's campaign is trying to keep us at a distance. We tried to attend the luncheon that he is attending, today. Well, his campaign kicked us off the property and moved us all the way across the street. We don't know if we're going to get any closer.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We didn't. Walker slipped out. It comes less than 24 hours after the story broke. An anonymous woman claiming to the "Daily Beast" that when she became pregnant in 2009, Walker urged her to have an abortion. She showed the reporter a $575 bill from the abortion clinic and a $700 check she says was from Walker.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN SENATE NOMINEE FACES BOMBSHELL ALLEGATIONS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There's also this, a "get well soon" card she says he gave her. ABC News has not independently confirmed the report, but Walker says it never happened.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 I never asked anyone to get an abortion. I never paid for an abortion, and it's a lie.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And when asked about that $700 check.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 Well, I send money to a lot of people, and that's what's so funny. I give money to people all the time, because I'm always helping people, because I believe in being generous.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Walker opposes abortion rights in all cases, no exceptions.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (REP) (SENATORIAL CANDIDATE IN GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 I'm for life. In the Ten Commandments, does it not say, "Thou shalt not kill"? That's one of the Ten Commandments that you should live by, that we should go by, "Thou shalt not kill."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, his own son, Christian Walker, calling him out as a hypocrite.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIAN WALKER (SON OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Family values, people? He has four kids, four different women. Wasn't in the house raising one of them. He was out having sex with other women. Do you care about family values?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Christian Walker, a conservative influencer, with a large presence on social media, says every member of Walker's family had begged him not to run in the first place.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIAN WALKER (SON OF \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Don't lie about your life. You don't get to pretend you're some moral family guy. You don't get to pretend all these things. Do not lie.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott, with us live in Atlanta, tonight. Rachel, top Republicans standing by \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , tonight. And, of course, you don't need me to tell you, this is a key race, one of the few key Senate races that will determine who controls the Senate after the midterms. So, where does the race stand, tonight?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, David, and that is exactly why you are seeing Republicans on Capitol Hill rally behind \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With just five weeks to go until Election Day, polls show that this is a very tight race. And the Democrat, Senator Raphael Warnock, well, he is out on the campaign trail making it clear that he supports abortion rights, saying that Georgia voters have a real choice to make this November, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott, in Georgia, tonight. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020221005eia400003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FAMILY OF FOUR KIDNAPPED POLICE RELEASE IMAGES OF POSSIBLE SUSPECT\b0\par\par\uc2 190 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP, EMERGENCY APPEAL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALKER DENIES PAYING FOR ABORTION\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EAST COAST FLOOD ALERTS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, SEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHELTERS FILL AS DEATH TOLL RISES\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, SERIAL KILLER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW CASES TIED TO SERIAL KILLINGS\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIANS IN RETREAT\par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, MISSILE TEST, JAPAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: N. KOREA FIRES MISSILE OVER JAPAN\par \par \uc2 LYNN, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING LORETTA LYNN\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, KIDNAPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAMILY OF FOUR KIDNAPPED\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, authorities in Merced County, California in Northern California searching for four family members kidnapped.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The sheriff says a mother, a father, their 8-month-old daughter and her uncle were at a business when they were taken against their will. Authorities say there is no motive, no ransom demands. Police, tonight, releasing images of the possible suspect. He's believed to be armed and dangerous.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, here, Elon Musk's surprising turn in this \uc2 Twitter\uc2  war. And that new report on Tom Brady and Gisele.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020221005eia40000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP, EMERGENCY APPEAL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALKER DENIES PAYING FOR ABORTION\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EAST COAST FLOOD ALERTS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, SEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHELTERS FILL AS DEATH TOLL RISES\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, SERIAL KILLER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW CASES TIED TO SERIAL KILLINGS\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIANS IN RETREAT\par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, MISSILE TEST, JAPAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: N. KOREA FIRES MISSILE OVER JAPAN\par \par \uc2 LYNN, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING LORETTA LYNN\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, KIDNAPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAMILY OF FOUR KIDNAPPED\par \par \uc2 MUSK, TWITTER, BRADY, BUNDCHEN, DIVORCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To "The Index" of other news, tonight, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's purchase of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  appears to be back on track, tonight.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Musk, moving to avoid lawsuit from the company, now agreeing to go forward with the deal to buy \uc2 Twitter\uc2  for $44 billion. He tried to back out, claiming \uc2 Twitter\uc2  undercounted the number of fake accounts. He faced a $1 billion penalty for breaking the deal. Shares of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  soaring 22% on that news, today.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the report, tonight, on Tom Brady and his wife Gisele Bundchen.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "The New York Post" reporting both have hired divorce lawyers. The couple reportedly struggling after Brady decided to end his retirement. No comment yet from their representatives.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back here, tonight, Loretta Lynn, in her own words, how she wanted to be remembered.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020221005eia40000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT LIVE ON GMA ACTRESS TALKS ABOUT HER NEW MOVIE "TAR"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,281 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN'S DEVASTATING AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, MARCENO\par \par \uc2 IAN, DEVASTATION, DAMAGE, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, PUTIN, TROOPS, ANNEXATION, PETRAEUS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PUTIN, ANNEX, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 FREED, PRISONERS, EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA, GRINER\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, SOCCER, FIFA, STADIUM\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTINGS, VICTIMS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 WATT, CARDINALS, HEART, A-FIB, RHYTHM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP FROM "HOCUS POCUS 2"\par \par \uc2 HABERMAN, "NY TIMES", TRUMP, "CONFIDENCE MAN"\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, \uc2 NFL\uc2 , \uc2 NFLPA\uc2 , SMITH, SILLS, BELL\par \par \uc2 PUJOLS, HOME RUN, HONORED, RETIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, STORM SURGE, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, WOODS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, BREWSTER, SHAH, TREATMENT, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, THOMPSON, VALENTINE, HOWERIN\par \par \uc2 "POWER TRIP", BENSON, ELECTION FRAUD\par \par \uc2 SCREENING, BREAST CANCER, LEWIS, STENARD, PEARLMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 BLANCHETT, "TAR", HOSS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm here now with two-time Academy Award winner Cate Blanchett getting rave reviews, standing ovations for her new role in a new movie "Tar." Welcome back to "GMA."\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Thank you, George.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CATE BLANCHETT LIVE ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's get things out of the way right at the start, this is not a movie about dark, sticky coal byproducts.\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 No. But that would be one that I would go and see.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, yes.\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 No. It is not. It is not. It is not. No, it's about Lydia Tar, the eponymous, the woman who's in the title. And she's a maestro, she's a consummate musician. She's a composer and a conductor. And so, she's in a position of great cultural power. And the moment we find her in the movie, she's having her greatest triumph, but all of these undealt things in her past come back and haunt her. So, it all starts to fall apart.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It comes out later this week, I cannot wait to see it. And I was reading about your preparation for this movie, you've studied German.\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You studied piano and, of course, you learned how to conduct. What was the hardest?\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Gosh. I mean, look, it was a joy to do actually. I mean, with every pregnancy, I mean, I said I would go back and pick up piano again, because I learned as a girl. But it was probably the moment of stepping in front of Dresden Philharmonic, and...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And conducted for real?\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, that was, and it was a life-changing moment for me. A friend of mine who was helping me with the conducting, you know, to beat. You know, you beat with one hand and you shape the sound with another, you know, which is a bit like doing this, you know, I haven't done before. She said, you won't be prepared for the sound that comes at you with those big orchestral works. And it was, it was phenomenal.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What is the heart of the conductor skill?\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 I think it, Bernstein said it, it's breathing. You know that you get the down beat with the in breath and the out breath is the music. And the thing with the conductor is, we see them in performance and it looks like, what are they doing?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, exactly. That's what I asked.\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 But their presence often elicits, you know, their musical experience, you know, their pedigree, their understanding of the score and the history, it brings out a certain tone. And if you listen, as I did, to many different recordings, because Mahler, Mahler's Fifth Symphony is the center of the movie, you can hear the difference between the different conductors, they bring different sounds out. So...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What do you think you brought to it?\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 A certain magic. A je ne sais quoi. I don't know. I hope audiences who see it in the cinema will be able to hear that. But it's a rehearsal movie.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's give everybody a look.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "TAR"\par \par \uc2 NINA HOSS (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Imagine her (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Don't you dare defend her. She'll come and go lumping back. I've got a damn phone like every robot. How hard can it be to text all day?\par \par \uc2 NINA HOSS (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Oh, slow down or let me out.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As we saw, you also did your own driving.\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 When you play a concert musician, a conductor and you do not expect to go on a Formula 1 race car and drive the latest model electric \uc2 Porsche\uc2  and then shut down half of Berlin and do stunt driving, which is what we did with Nina Hoss, the wonderful Nina Hoss, who plays my character's partner.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Was that part fun?\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 That was really fun. It was, I think that was a genuine scream on Nina's behalf. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, I also read that Todd Field, the director, said that he would not have done this movie if you weren't available to do it. How much pressure does that add?\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Well, luckily, I didn't know that until the press notes because I might not have come out of my hole. You know, it was, look, that's an incredible compliment. We've met ten years ago. He was working on a piece with Joan Didion and, for one reason or another, because Todd is an incredibly rare and special director and he doesn't leave the bond unless he has something to say.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. He doesn't work that often.\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 No. And so, it's been 16 years since his last movie, "Little Children." And so, I've longed wanted to work with him. So, that's what I, yeah, that's why I work with him.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're also, I also just found out, you're going be in a new series, a part of this docuseries, Documentary Now?\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Yes, where I play a terrible hairdresser. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this was your idea?\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, yeah. I had seen this cute, they spoof documentaries. And it's a really beautiful documentary about these hairdressers in northern England, and I thought it was ripe for reinvention. So, yeah, that was fun.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Conducting to hairdressing.\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Yes, I know. Look, I'm really good at it.\par \par \uc2 STAFF MEMBER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 That's who you are.\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got Eddie's approval, it's okay.\par \par \uc2 CATE BLANCHETT (ACTRESS "TAR")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. But you're beyond help, I'm sorry. There's nothing much I can do there.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you for coming in. "Tar" is going to be in select theaters this Friday, opens nationwide on October 28th. And coming up, we're going to continue our kick off with Breast Cancer Awareness Month and tell you what you need to know about early detection.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia30000q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BATTLING BREAST CANCER THE LATEST IN RESEARCH, TREATMENT & PREVENTION\b0\par\par\uc2 1,796 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN'S DEVASTATING AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, MARCENO\par \par \uc2 IAN, DEVASTATION, DAMAGE, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, PUTIN, TROOPS, ANNEXATION, PETRAEUS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PUTIN, ANNEX, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 FREED, PRISONERS, EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA, GRINER\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, SOCCER, FIFA, STADIUM\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTINGS, VICTIMS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 WATT, CARDINALS, HEART, A-FIB, RHYTHM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP FROM "HOCUS POCUS 2"\par \par \uc2 HABERMAN, "NY TIMES", TRUMP, "CONFIDENCE MAN"\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, \uc2 NFL\uc2 , \uc2 NFLPA\uc2 , SMITH, SILLS, BELL\par \par \uc2 PUJOLS, HOME RUN, HONORED, RETIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, STORM SURGE, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, WOODS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, BREWSTER, SHAH, TREATMENT, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Back here. We're kicking off our Breast Cancer Awareness Month series, thriving in pink. And we are surrounded by the faces of some incredible breast cancer thrivers. Thanks to the breast cancer organization Susan G. Komen for these images of strength. And this morning, we're looking at the latest advancements in the fight against the disease.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLING BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE LATEST ADVANCEMENTS IN RESEARCH, TREATMENT & PREVENTION\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Joining us are two specialists Dr. Abenaa Brewster, an oncologist at MD Anderson Cancer Center, and Dr. Ami Shah, oncologist at \uc2 Lurie Cancer Center\uc2  at Northwestern Medicine. I enjoyed talking with you during the commercial break, and just so, so grateful for what's going on. And I want to start with you, Dr. Brewster, because studies show, during the pandemic, nearly 47% of people, they did not have their breast cancer screenings and that has led to later diagnoses. So, what is your message for them this morning.\par \par \uc2 DR ABENAA BREWSTER (BREAST MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 Robin, you're absolutely right. And I have patients in my practice who, for different reasons, didn't get a mammogram during the pandemic and now are being treated for later stage of the disease. And so, I cannot emphasize enough the importance of women getting back in and getting their regular screening mammograms. We know that early detection with a mammogram improves survival.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PANDEMIC IMPACT ON BREAST CANCER DIAGNOSIS\par \par \uc2 DR ABENAA BREWSTER (BREAST MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 At MD Anderson, we recommend that women start screening at age 40 and have a mammogram once a year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER SCREENING RECOMMENDATIONS\par \par \uc2 DR ABENAA BREWSTER (BREAST MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 And if women are high risk that they have a mammogram and an MRI, alternating every six months. And most women have no idea if they're an average or high risk of developing breast cancer. So, I encourage women to have that discussion with their physician. The physician will review their risk factors, review their family history. They may even order genetic testing because there are so many more genes that have been identified that can contribute to breast cancer risk. So, I would encourage women. The bottom line is, it's time to get back to regular screening mammograms and having that discussion with your physician to determine what is your risk of developing breast cancer, what type of screening you should get and the timing of the screening.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. And I have to say, men also, men also with breast cancer. We hear this every time we do a segment like this. Okay, Dr. Shah, treatments. I mean, there have been some advancements as well. Right?\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CTR OF NORTHWESTERN MED)\par \par \uc2 Yes, there's a lot to be excited about. For triple negative breast cancer, immunotherapy has been an important development. This is the type of medication activates our own immune system to better recognize cancer cells.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TREATMENT OPTIONS FOR TRIPLE NEGATIVE BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CTR OF NORTHWESTERN MED)\par \par \uc2 And in doing so, we better jobs of treating the cancer. For those with stage 2 and 3 triple negative breast cancer, adding immunotherapy to chemotherapy creates better responses, results in fewer recurrences and it's going to cure more patients. And it also benefits those in a subgroup of triple negative breast cancer that have metastatic disease.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh.\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CTR OF NORTHWESTERN MED)\par \par \uc2 We've also seen the development of category of drugs called antibody drug conjugates. And these drugs, they take chemotherapy and they connect it to an antibody. That antibody serves as a guide through the body, trying to bring that chemotherapy in higher levels to the cancers and less to the rest of the body. Hopefully sparing some of the undesired side effects and getting better responses with the tumor.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CTR OF NORTHWESTERN MED)\par \par \uc2 And so, we're only scratching the surface of the potential of those medications.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Only scratching the surface. You brought up metastatic, and I do want to talk about that in just a moment. But first of all, Dr. Brewster, we have seen that different ethnic and racial groups, it affects differently. So, can you just talk about the differences?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLING BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DISPARITIES BETWEEN ETHNIC & RACIAL GROUPS\par \par \uc2 DR ABENAA BREWSTER (BREAST MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. So, black women, and I would say particularly younger black women have about a two to three-fold higher risk of developing triple negative breast cancers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK WOMEN & TRIPLE NEGATIVE BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 DR ABENAA BREWSTER (BREAST MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 And triple negative breast cancers are an aggressive type of breast cancer. So, we want to catch it early in order to give women the best chances of being cured. And so, I would recommend that black women have a mammogram every year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRIPLE-NEGATIVE BREAST CANCER TESTS NEGATIVE FOR ESTROGEN, PROGESTERONE AND HER2\par \par \uc2 DR ABENAA BREWSTER (BREAST MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 And if you feel a lump in your breast, to bring it to attention to their physician sooner rather than later to get it checked out.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRIPLE-NEGATIVE BREAST CANCER MORE AGGRESSIVE THAN OTHER FORMS\par \par \uc2 DR ABENAA BREWSTER (BREAST MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 We don't fully understand why black women have this higher risk of developing triple negative breast cancers, but we know that when black women have equal access to early detection and equal access to some of the state-of-the-art treatments that Dr. Shah mentioned, they have a similar prognosis from triple negative breast cancer as white women.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, my goodness. I remember when I was diagnosed with triple negative and had to go through radiation and chemotherapy and the surgery, but to think of the advancements from then to now. But there are still some communities, Dr. Shah, that screening just is not in their mindset to do. Why do you think that is?\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CTR OF NORTHWESTERN MED)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I think there's a lot of things that are barriers or misconceptions that lead to people not getting screening. I think one thing we hear all too often is, I don't have a family history. My mother never had a mammogram. You know, I've lived a healthy life, it won't affect me. And, unfortunately, that's just not true. one in eight women will be diagnosed with invasive breast cancer in their lifetime. And so, it's important that everybody, including those with average risk get regular screening mammogram.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And can we talk about metastatic breast cancer because, so often, it's a group that's overlooked. And it, you know, it's not one size fits all, there are different types of breast cancer. But metastatic, it is so different from the others.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TREATMENT FOR LATER STAGE METASTATIC BREAST CANCERS VS. EARLIER TYPES\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CTR OF NORTHWESTERN MED)\par \par \uc2 It's true. Metastatic breast cancer is when the cancer has traveled outside of the breast and the immediate lymph nodes to other parts of the body. And it is a type of breast cancer where a majority of patients, we don't have cures, but we absolutely have treatments. And those treatments are advancing very quickly. As we talked about some of the new exciting medications in that area, there's much more in the pipeline. And that's where people's research dollars and patients' willingness to participate in clinical trials has really made some important strides.\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CTR OF NORTHWESTERN MED)\par \par \uc2 And we're looking at studying the tumor or studying DNA, fragmented DNA in your bloodstream that could help guide us to match the right treatment. And so, those research, that research will hopefully translate into better and better outcomes because we see patients every day with all stages with metastatic breast cancer who are thriving.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I saw a woman outside with Amy in the group and she was like defiant. She's like, I'm going to keep fighting. I'm going to keep fighting.\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CTR OF NORTHWESTERN MED)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But what are some other ways that can help prevent breast cancer?\par \par \uc2 DR ABENAA BREWSTER (BREAST MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 Well, you know, we all know that saying, an ounce of prevention is worth a pound of cure. And so, there's been great news in prevention.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW PREVENTION OPTIONS ARE AVAILABLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW CANCER PREVENTION OPTIONS\par \par \uc2 DR ABENAA BREWSTER (BREAST MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST MD ANDERSON CANCER CTR)\par \par \uc2 Over the past decade, we've been using preventive therapy, which are essentially estrogen-blocking pills that women take about five years that could reduce their risk of developing a breast cancer by about half. And these pills are usually recommended for women who are at high risk of developing breast cancer. And that means women who have a strong family history of breast cancer or who may have a type of benign breast lesion that puts them at increased risk. The majority of women who take these pills do very well. But there are some side effects, particularly for the pill called tamoxifen. And so, having a discussion with your physician and finding out whether or not you're a candidate for preventive therapy, I would certainly recommend for women who are at high risk.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dr. Brewster, Dr. Shah, wonderful to meet you both. Thank you for your tireless efforts and the work that you do.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia30000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAST CANCER IN YOUNG WOMEN YOUNG THRIVERS TAKING TO SOCIAL MEDIA TO SHARE THEIR STORIES\b0\par\par\uc2 932 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN'S DEVASTATING AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, MARCENO\par \par \uc2 IAN, DEVASTATION, DAMAGE, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, PUTIN, TROOPS, ANNEXATION, PETRAEUS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PUTIN, ANNEX, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 FREED, PRISONERS, EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA, GRINER\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, SOCCER, FIFA, STADIUM\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTINGS, VICTIMS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 WATT, CARDINALS, HEART, A-FIB, RHYTHM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP FROM "HOCUS POCUS 2"\par \par \uc2 HABERMAN, "NY TIMES", TRUMP, "CONFIDENCE MAN"\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, \uc2 NFL\uc2 , \uc2 NFLPA\uc2 , SMITH, SILLS, BELL\par \par \uc2 PUJOLS, HOME RUN, HONORED, RETIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, STORM SURGE, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, WOODS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, BREWSTER, SHAH, TREATMENT, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, THOMPSON, VALENTINE, HOWERIN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we know it's also affecting younger folks. And so, T.J. and George are going to talk about that.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, you know, that jumps out, right? They say, recommendation for women starting at 40, but there are women in their 20s and 30s who are getting diagnosed. And some are now taking to social media to try to raise awareness. Our Stephanie Ramos, excuse me, has that for us. Stephanie, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER IN YOUNG WOMEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUNG THRIVERS TAKING TO SOCIAL MEDIA TO SHARE THEIR STORIES\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, T.J. As you know, breast cancer is the most common cancer in women in this country. And these young women you're about to hear from are sharing their stories that could have a major impact on someone else's life.\par \par \uc2 CANCER SURVIVOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I was recently diagnosed with stage 3 breast cancer at the age of 29.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) These young women in their 20s and 30s taking to social media with a shocking diagnosis, breast cancer. While it's rare, new research shows breast cancer in women under 50 is on the rise and, with it, bringing a unique set of circumstances.\par \par \uc2 DR MARGARET THOMPSON (BREAST ONCOLOGY SURGEON CLEVELAND CLINIC)\par \par \uc2 They're just starting their careers, they're starting their families, they have their whole life ahead of them.\par \par \uc2 DIAMONIQUE VALENTINE (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER AT AGE 27)\par \par \uc2 We are at chemo for round two.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Entrepreneur Diamonique Valentine was just 27 when she shared her diagnosis on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , stage 3 triple negative, found in black women under 40 at higher rates than in other races.\par \par \uc2 DIAMONIQUE VALENTINE (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER AT AGE 27)\par \par \uc2 I didn't think that cancer was something that could happen to me. I also thought that it had to run in your family. At that moment I was diagnosed, it was like, you have cancer, okay, you're going to die.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She found her own lump as did Alexis Howerin, at the time just 21 years old and a college student, then facing stage 2 cancer.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS HOWERIN (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER AT 21)\par \par \uc2 It was gut-wrenching. The only thing I knew about cancer was it took my grandmother's life. So, immediately, I thought, oh, my life is pretty much over.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While the risk is low, young women often face breast cancers that can be more aggressive and more difficult to treat.\par \par \uc2 DR MARGARET THOMPSON (BREAST ONCOLOGY SURGEON CLEVELAND CLINIC)\par \par \uc2 In younger aged women, their biology of the tumor tends to present with more aggressive features compared to post-menopausal women.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Young breast tissue tends to be dense, so it can be difficult to see tumors even on mammograms. And because breast cancer in young people is rare, it may be misdiagnosed. Diamonique says being a better self-advocate could have gotten here a diagnosis months sooner.\par \par \uc2 DIAMONIQUE VALENTINE (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER AT AGE 27)\par \par \uc2 I wish that I would have advocated a little bit more and was a little bit more diligent in finding someone who would screen me with no insurance. So, I went from August to October when it probably could have been stage 1 or 2 all the way to stage 3.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Another unique circumstance, young women can also face infertility from harsh cancer treatments.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS HOWERIN (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER AT 21)\par \par \uc2 I always dreamt of being a mother. One of my biggest goals in life is to have my own kids.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Alexis says she changed her treatment timeline in order to freeze her eggs. Diamonique says she felt the costs were too high. She and her husband Marcus hoped for the best.\par \par \uc2 DIAMONIQUE'S HUSBAND (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Whatever happens, happens. We have each other. That was the decision that we made together and here we are.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Baby boy Mali (PH) was born in May.\par \par \uc2 DIAMONIQUE VALENTINE (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER AT AGE 27)\par \par \uc2 He's everything that me and my family needed. It's like the reward after the storm. Nothing makes me more grateful.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we've got more fantastic news, both women are now cancer free. And they want other women to know that checking your own breast could be the difference between life and death for young women, especially since breast cancer screenings aren't always made available for women under the age of 40. T.J.?\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it's great to see their stories. They absolutely are doing a service. Thank you so much, Steph.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia30000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 08:00 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 797 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN'S DEVASTATING AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, MARCENO\par \par \uc2 IAN, DEVASTATION, DAMAGE, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, PUTIN, TROOPS, ANNEXATION, PETRAEUS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PUTIN, ANNEX, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 FREED, PRISONERS, EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA, GRINER\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, SOCCER, FIFA, STADIUM\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTINGS, VICTIMS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 WATT, CARDINALS, HEART, A-FIB, RHYTHM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP FROM "HOCUS POCUS 2"\par \par \uc2 HABERMAN, "NY TIMES", TRUMP, "CONFIDENCE MAN"\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, NFL, \uc2 NFLPA\uc2 , SMITH, SILLS, BELL\par \par \uc2 PUJOLS, HOME RUN, HONORED, RETIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America, it's 8:00 AM.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE IAN AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH FOR SURVIVORS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Search for survivors in Florida underway as the death toll from Hurricane Ian rises. At least 83 people killed in the storm, more than 1,600 rescued. Many more still stranded. This morning, the extent of the damage as questions grow about the evacuation orders and whether they came soon enough.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN'S AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEIGHBORS HELPING NEIGHBORS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Neighbors helping neighbors in the aftermath of Hurricane Ian. The close-knit community of Harlem Heights coming together after the food pantry that served hundreds was flooded and the volunteers coming to help in this time of need.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIVE ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CATE BLANCHETT!\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oscar winner Cate Blanchett is live in Times Square, talking about her new movie and the challenges she took on to perfect the part.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER AWARENESS MONTH\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Thriving in pink. This morning, we kick off Breast Cancer Awareness Month, the latest on the cutting-edge science in detection and treatment that could save lives. Plus, the young women stunned by their diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 DIAMONIQUE VALENTINE (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER AT AGE 27)\par \par \uc2 I didn't think that cancer was something that could happen to me.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Taking to social media to share their stories. And what those still fighting breast cancer want others to know.\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Just make sure that you're checking yourself, ladies, because this is nothing to play with.\par \par \uc2 SARA KLOSTERBOER (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 If something doesn't feel right, go get it checked out. It just might save your life.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How your own journey could help save someone else's life.\par \par \uc2 MELITZA SANTIAGO (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I want to share hope with those fighting breast cancer that you're not alone.\par \par \uc2 BRETT FELDER (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I want you to know that, for every second that you're fighting your battle, you're encouraging someone else to fight theirs.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 This morning, the surprise we have for two women, turning their tragedy into triumph, saving as many lives as they can as we say...\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Ginger was out with them as well with her pink suit. I'm telling you. Good morning, America. We appreciate you being with us. It is October, which means Breast Cancer Awareness Month, so wonderful to have those inspiring messages from the thrivers and we have a lot more ahead.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It is Breast Cancer Awareness Month, but one in eight women, that's still staggering to think that one in eight women will be diagnosed with breast cancer at some point. Now, we have some folks right there, I've got Jean and Irene here, they're part of a team that runs the Mount Sinai mobile mammography van. And let's head outside for a second. Robes is out there. Robes, we've got something special planned for them today.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes, T.J. You can hear all the cheering here. I'm here with some survivors and the warriors who are still fighting this disease. And when it comes to any type of cancer, we know that early detection is so important. It was obviously a big part of my own story. And we're about to celebrate two women who help give people access to those always important screenings. And that's all coming up, guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And thank you so much, Amy. Amy was the one who got in that van.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I remember that day.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She got into that van, she had never had...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Right here.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Right, had never had a mammogram before and it led to her diagnosis and look at her now.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She's doing great. We are looking forward to seeing more of this.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia30000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MEET THE WOMEN OF THE "MAMMO VAN" CELEBRATING THE UNSUNG HEROES OF BREAST CANCER BATTLE\b0\par\par\uc2 2,499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN'S DEVASTATING AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, MARCENO\par \par \uc2 IAN, DEVASTATION, DAMAGE, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, PUTIN, TROOPS, ANNEXATION, PETRAEUS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PUTIN, ANNEX, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 FREED, PRISONERS, EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA, GRINER\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, SOCCER, FIFA, STADIUM\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTINGS, VICTIMS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 WATT, CARDINALS, HEART, A-FIB, RHYTHM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP FROM "HOCUS POCUS 2"\par \par \uc2 HABERMAN, "NY TIMES", TRUMP, "CONFIDENCE MAN"\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, \uc2 NFL\uc2 , \uc2 NFLPA\uc2 , SMITH, SILLS, BELL\par \par \uc2 PUJOLS, HOME RUN, HONORED, RETIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, STORM SURGE, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, WOODS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, BREWSTER, SHAH, TREATMENT, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, THOMPSON, VALENTINE, HOWERIN\par \par \uc2 "POWER TRIP", BENSON, ELECTION FRAUD\par \par \uc2 SCREENING, BREAST CANCER, LEWIS, STENARD, PEARLMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "GMA." Yes, we are kicking off Breast Cancer Awareness Month with these good folks that you see here. We are celebrating the lives of those who have been affected by the disease. We have a special surprise, that's why I'm talking like this, because we're surprising a couple of people who are right outside the door, two amazing women. Robach is here with me now. This is incredible to see Robin and George, everybody remembers you on the air that morning, years ago, you stepped outside in this very thing and had a breast cancer screening. It kind of changed the course of your life.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It absolutely changed the course of my life. It was nine years ago that Robin Roberts convinced me to walk into that mammo van. I thought the breast cancer couldn't happen to me.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) I just had turned 40. And sure enough, it turned into a stage 2 breast cancer diagnosis. And it was all because of "Good Morning America," and it was all because of Breast Cancer Awareness Month, it brought that experience to me.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we know, that early detection made possible by vans like those mammo vans. The Mount Sinai mobile mammography van, which has saved lives, countless lives, they give people, women easy access to mammograms, the mammograms come to them. So many women of color have trouble getting a proper screening. And, of course, what T.J. just mentioned, it was a mammo van that led to my diagnosis. So, it is a cause near and dear to my heart. The Mount Sinai van has caught 30 breast cancers after screening about 6,000 people. There are two women here that you just mentioned, Jean and Irene, that's why we're talking softly.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go to them. They have turned their own deeply personal experience into a force for change. So, I'm going to head right out here to Jean and Irene, they're standing right here in this beautiful pink bed of roses or flowers that we have here. Hi, welcome.\par \par \uc2 IRENE PEARLMAN (VOLUNTEER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 Hi, thank you so much. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So lovely to have you both. You two are literally saving lives each and every day. And I know that you're both really passionate about it, come with me here, because of how breast cancer just touch both of your lives. You both have stories. And I think you're here, of course, you think you're here to promote breast cancer awareness, right?\par \par \uc2 IRENE PEARLMAN (VOLUNTEER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 And we are.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. You're here for that, yes. But I know you've been through a lot of obstacles to get here. Your mammo van actually broke down this morning for the first time ever, that's never happened before. But, of course, that happened today. I want you both to come with me because look what we have here. We want to celebrate you. They're greeting their friends here and the amazing work that you have done. We want to celebrate you. You can see, come over here, ladies. Look at all these people who came out to support you. Irene, your son Seth is here. Oh, yeah, there he is.\par \par \uc2 IRENE PEARLMAN (VOLUNTEER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 I didn't see you. I didn't see you.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, he did actually let you know. Oh, my goodness. And then Jean, your co-workers are here who are like your family, I know. Each and every day you work with them.\par \par \uc2 JEAN STENARD (MANAGER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Early detection, we were talking about it so important when it comes to cancer, it prevents cancer deaths, we all know that.\par \par \uc2 JEAN STENARD (MANAGER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the Mount Sinai van is a huge part of that, screening up to 2,000 people per year. We know your story, but now it's time for America to learn your stories. Let's take a look.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEET THE WOMEN OF THE "MAMMO VAN"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING THE UNSUNG HEROES OF BREAST CANCER BATTLE\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's a mammogram on wheels, Mount Sinai mammo van bringing the technology across five boroughs of New York City. The goal? To reach as many women as possible and catch breast cancer early.\par \par \uc2 DR LAURIE MARGOLIES (CHIEF OF BREAST IMAGING MOUNT SINAI HEALTH SYSTEM)\par \par \uc2 We need people not to be afraid of breast cancer. We need people not to be afraid of mammograms.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The backbone of this mammo van, program manager Jean Stenard.\par \par \uc2 DR LAURIE MARGOLIES (CHIEF OF BREAST IMAGING MOUNT SINAI HEALTH SYSTEM)\par \par \uc2 Jean runs this van. She's the glue that hold us together.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER LEWIS (LEAD DRIVER SITE-VEHICLE OPERATIONS COORDINATOR)\par \par \uc2 She's very courteous, very generous and she always puts this program and the people in the program before herself.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For Jean, it's personal. Her mother, Helen, died of breast cancer in the '90s and she has made it her mission to help others.\par \par \uc2 DR LAURIE MARGOLIES (CHIEF OF BREAST IMAGING MOUNT SINAI HEALTH SYSTEM)\par \par \uc2 In 2022, we're going to do almost 2,000 mammograms. We're going to find many cancers. We're going to really help people and save lives.\par \par \uc2 BONNIE LAUBE (BEST FRIEND OF JEAN)\par \par \uc2 This is a topic that's near and dear to her heart and she has worked tirelessly. She is the heart and soul.\par \par \uc2 PAUL STENARD (BROTHER OF JEAN)\par \par \uc2 I know she spends many more hours than she's expected to and that's always kind of been her nature.\par \par \uc2 SARA STENARD (NIECE OF JEAN)\par \par \uc2 She really cares about the cause and about breast cancer awareness.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jean training volunteers like Irene Pearlman who joined the mammogram van to honor her late sister, Phyllis.\par \par \uc2 LUCILLE TONER (COLLEAGUE OF IRENE)\par \par \uc2 Irene is very warm, very kind, very caring.\par \par \uc2 DR LAURIE MARGOLIES (CHIEF OF BREAST IMAGING MOUNT SINAI HEALTH SYSTEM)\par \par \uc2 She reached out and she said, I would really love to help get more women screened.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Marking the 30 years since her sister's passing from breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 JOANN COFFIN (VP OF QUALITY & REGULATORY AFFAIRS / IRENE'S BOSS)\par \par \uc2 To bring this service to women who need it, in her sister's memory, it's wonderful.\par \par \uc2 FRIEND (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It is so important to her.\par \par \uc2 SETH PEARLMAN (SON OF IRENE)\par \par \uc2 It's honestly a beautiful thing for Aunt Phyllis. And I'm sure she's literally looking down and smiling and saying, what a beautiful sister I have.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both Jean and Irene honoring their loved ones daily by helping to save lives.\par \par \uc2 SARA STENARD (NIECE OF JEAN)\par \par \uc2 We love you so much, Auntie Jean, and we're so proud of you.\par \par \uc2 EMILY STENARD (NIECE OF JEAN)\par \par \uc2 It's more than, more than, more than deserved.\par \par \uc2 FRIEND (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Good job, my friend.\par \par \uc2 RICHARD GRIESCHE (FRIEND OF JEAN)\par \par \uc2 Enjoy the moment, Jean. So well deserved.\par \par \uc2 LUCILLE TONER (COLLEAGUE OF IRENE)\par \par \uc2 Irene, you know, is such an advocate for getting screened.\par \par \uc2 GREGORY PEARLMAN (SON OF IRENE)\par \par \uc2 Thank you for being the best mom and the best leader for doing something that's going to be greatly beneficial for a lot of women out there in the community.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We could see, we could see the emotion both of your faces because you do so much, but it's so nice to see you both of you celebrated. It's so important for all of your work. And, Jean, as we saw in story, you lost your mom to breast cancer and it made you want to give back. And I love that you made your mess your message. That's what Robin Roberts always says to do. And you take so much time off taking care of others and want to know what it's like for you in this moment to feel that love returned, to feel celebrated.\par \par \uc2 JEAN STENARD (MANAGER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 I am just so touched by this. It's just wonderful to be joining all of you in focusing on this really important topic. And it means so much to me, I just can't thank you enough for doing this.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And like you said, focusing on the topic, I know you all are probably a little bit uncomfortable with the focus being on you both and the work that you're doing.\par \par \uc2 JEAN STENARD (MANAGER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 You bet.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Irene, we mentioned there, you lost your mom and your sister, your sister was 30 years ago, Phyllis, I think.\par \par \uc2 IRENE PEARLMAN (VOLUNTEER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was the, I assume they're with you every single day of your work. What do you think they think about what you're doing?\par \par \uc2 IRENE PEARLMAN (VOLUNTEER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 I walk with them every day, they are always with me. They would be so proud. Really, the message, I feel like I'm always their voice, right? Their voices are stilled. So, what's their voice? Their voice would say, please try and get screened. Please try and make sure this disease doesn't happen to you, that you can get early detection, treatment, that families aren't so sad and saddened by what happened. So, they would be really just pleased.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, well, someone who's pleased as well, his son Seth. You didn't know he was there.\par \par \uc2 SETH PEARLMAN (SON OF IRENE)\par \par \uc2 I didn't. Because he was at the end of the line. I didn't see him.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot going on.\par \par \uc2 IRENE PEARLMAN (VOLUNTEER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 I know, a lot. I mean, I didn't expect everyone.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we heard some of it there on the piece, but you tell us what it means to see your mom do, we see her this morning. America see her this morning. You see her every day doing this work.\par \par \uc2 SETH PEARLMAN (SON OF IRENE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, that's pretty crazy. She literally, she does this every day. This is part of her culture, her lifestyle and just that the world knows about it now is definitely a beautiful thing because literally every day this is just who she is as a person. So, it's definitely a beautiful thing, mom.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You are both huge inspirations because I always talk about the power of one voice it can change someone's mind. Like I'm going to take my health seriously, I'm going to make that phone call, make that appointment, keep that appointment.\par \par \uc2 JEAN STENARD (MANAGER MOUNT SINAI MOBILE MAMMOGRAPHY VAN)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, everything you do affects so many people that you don't even know about it. I want to bring in Laurie, you're the chief of radiology at Mount Sinai. You oversee the van program and you actually nominated Irene and Jean to be celebrated this morning. Talk a little bit about what the impact is, these two women make on your organization.\par \par \uc2 DR LAURIE MARGOLIES (CHIEF OF BREAST IMAGING MOUNT SINAI HEALTH SYSTEM)\par \par \uc2 So, both Irene and Jean have very, very similar impacts in that they help bring screening mammograms to people who might be afraid to get them otherwise, who might have barriers to go, just like you found that there was some reason why you didn't make an appointment at one of fixed sites that are obviously available to you. But having that mobile van in your community takes away a barrier, not needing a prescription takes away a huge barrier, being able to come sometimes without an appointment takes away a huge barrier. So, by breaking down those walls, both Irene and Jean help save women's lives and they do it every day and they give of themselves above and beyond.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yay. People are scared, they're scared of the pain, they're scared of the results. And when you break those barriers down, it does save lives and it's been proven. So, that's incredible. Jean, we have another surprise that you don't even know about it. Jean and Laurie, we have a surprise that you don't even know about, all of you. This is an exciting one. Jewelry designer Kendra Scott heard about what you're doing, she's also very passionate about your mission, she's an incredible advocate for breast cancer and breast cancer research. She is donating $20,000 to your organization. Tell us what this money will mean in terms of how and who you can help.\par \par \uc2 DR LAURIE MARGOLIES (CHIEF OF BREAST IMAGING MOUNT SINAI HEALTH SYSTEM)\par \par \uc2 So, what this money means is that people who don't have insurance or people that are underinsured will be able to get screening mammograms without worrying about a bill coming in the mail.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Congratulations to all of you and thank you, again, for all that you do to help women everywhere to have access to mammograms. I always say, they're not perfect but they're the best, best test we have to treat breast cancer, to detect it and then to save lives. So, thank you all so much. And coming up, we have Cate Blanchett. She's with us live in Times Square. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia30000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW LOOK AT "POWER TRIP" EMBED REPORTERS ASKING TOUGH QUESTIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN'S DEVASTATING AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, MARCENO\par \par \uc2 IAN, DEVASTATION, DAMAGE, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, PUTIN, TROOPS, ANNEXATION, PETRAEUS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PUTIN, ANNEX, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 FREED, PRISONERS, EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA, GRINER\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, SOCCER, FIFA, STADIUM\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTINGS, VICTIMS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 WATT, CARDINALS, HEART, A-FIB, RHYTHM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP FROM "HOCUS POCUS 2"\par \par \uc2 HABERMAN, "NY TIMES", TRUMP, "CONFIDENCE MAN"\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, \uc2 NFL\uc2 , \uc2 NFLPA\uc2 , SMITH, SILLS, BELL\par \par \uc2 PUJOLS, HOME RUN, HONORED, RETIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, STORM SURGE, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, WOODS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, BREWSTER, SHAH, TREATMENT, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, THOMPSON, VALENTINE, HOWERIN\par \par \uc2 "POWER TRIP", BENSON, ELECTION FRAUD\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the new episode of my Hulu docuseries "Power Trip: Those Who Seek Power and Those Who Chase Them." In this week's show, we see our young reporters chasing down stories about conspiracy theories and election threats. Secretaries of state on the front lines this year. In this clip, our embed reporter Paulina Tam questions one of those candidates in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW LOOK AT "POWER TRIP"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EMBED REPORTERS ASKING TOUGH QUESTIONS ON THE CAMPAIGN TRAIL\par \par \uc2 PAULINA TAM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) I think many voters know there's presidential race every four years, Senate race every two years, you know, House congressional races, two.\par \par \uc2 PAULINA TAM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is the entrance.\par \par \uc2 PAULINA TAM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But secretary of state races, not that many people know about that. Some voters don't even know what SOS, secretary of state, SOS is, and what they do. They are the chief election officers, so they certify the results.\par \par \uc2 PAULINA TAM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They oversee, making sure the election system is running smoothly. It will be interesting come November. I've spoken to quite a few voters as an embed covering three states. And they told me the two biggest issues on their mind when they head to the polls in November are election integrity and voter fraud. How is your office trying to safeguard the process now?\par \par \uc2 JOCELYN BENSON\uc2  (MICHIGAN SECRETARY OF STATE)\par \par \uc2 We've got work to do to address a sector of voters particularly in one political party who've been misled by their leaders who have spread misinformation, some knowingly so. So, a lot of our work is to make sure they know the truth and to be transparent.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's been so great to watch these young reporters grow, T.J. And I've got some advice for them from our Pulitzer Prize winner Maggie Haberman.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Which was?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She said, don't give up and don't take it personally when they say no.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Don't take it personal. She's right.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There you go. First two episodes of "Power Trip" available to stream now on \uc2 Hulu\uc2 . And the new episodes drop every Sunday.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And we are back here celebrating Breast Cancer Awareness Month with a surprise. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia30000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN'S DEVASTATING AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, MARCENO\par \par \uc2 IAN, DEVASTATION, DAMAGE, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, PUTIN, TROOPS, ANNEXATION, PETRAEUS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PUTIN, ANNEX, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 FREED, PRISONERS, EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA, GRINER\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, SOCCER, FIFA, STADIUM\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTINGS, VICTIMS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 WATT, CARDINALS, HEART, A-FIB, RHYTHM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP FROM "HOCUS POCUS 2"\par \par \uc2 HABERMAN, "NY TIMES", TRUMP, "CONFIDENCE MAN"\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, \uc2 NFL\uc2 , \uc2 NFLPA\uc2 , SMITH, SILLS, BELL\par \par \uc2 PUJOLS, HOME RUN, HONORED, RETIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, STORM SURGE, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, WOODS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, BREWSTER, SHAH, TREATMENT, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, THOMPSON, VALENTINE, HOWERIN\par \par \uc2 "POWER TRIP", BENSON, ELECTION FRAUD\par \par \uc2 SCREENING, BREAST CANCER, LEWIS, STENARD, PEARLMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, welcome back to "GMA." I'm here with thrivers and volunteers at \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2 , whose courage we are celebrating this morning. We have something special to honor them as well, and it is some thriver forecast. Look at some of the cities.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVER FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, we came up with a little forecast, Thrive City, California mid-60s and sunny. Victory Township, Michigan, 64. And Survivors Hill, California. Now, can you all do your survivor pose with me.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Give a little something like, uh-huh. This is what we got. Sachi (PH) and I are fully matching in the pink suits. We are so grateful for you all being here. Let's go ahead and check a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia30000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SELF-EXAM 101 WITH "THE BREASTIES" THE IMPORTANCE OF EARLY DETECTION\b0\par\par\uc2 1,059 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN'S DEVASTATING AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, MARCENO\par \par \uc2 IAN, DEVASTATION, DAMAGE, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, PUTIN, TROOPS, ANNEXATION, PETRAEUS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PUTIN, ANNEX, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 FREED, PRISONERS, EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA, GRINER\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, SOCCER, FIFA, STADIUM\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTINGS, VICTIMS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 WATT, CARDINALS, HEART, A-FIB, RHYTHM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP FROM "HOCUS POCUS 2"\par \par \uc2 HABERMAN, "NY TIMES", TRUMP, "CONFIDENCE MAN"\par \par \uc2 TAGOVAILOA, \uc2 NFL\uc2 , \uc2 NFLPA\uc2 , SMITH, SILLS, BELL\par \par \uc2 PUJOLS, HOME RUN, HONORED, RETIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, STORM SURGE, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, WOODS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, BREWSTER, SHAH, TREATMENT, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, THOMPSON, VALENTINE, HOWERIN\par \par \uc2 "POWER TRIP", BENSON, ELECTION FRAUD\par \par \uc2 SCREENING, BREAST CANCER, LEWIS, STENARD, PEARLMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 BLANCHETT, "TAR", HOSS\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, DETECTION, GROSS, PELED, EXAM\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now with our kickoff of Breast Cancer Awareness Month. One of the keys to treating breast cancer successfully is finding it early. So, this morning, we're going to show you how to do a self-exam with the help of Kelly Gross and Dr. Anne Peled from an organization that we love called The Breasties. Welcome. So, first, I'll ask you, Kelly, tell me about The Breasties.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SELF-EXAM 101 WITH "THE BREASTIES"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE IMPORTANCE OF EARLY DETECTION\par \par \uc2 KELLIE GROSS (DIRECTOR OF DIVERSITY EQUITY & INCLUSION "THE BREASTIES")\par \par \uc2 Yes, I'm so excited to share that with you. The Breasties is an organization that is primed to support anyone that has been impacted by breast and gynecological cancers. And what we are mostly is community. We want to make sure that the community is supported. We want to build a space where everyone feels included, welcome and supported and, most of all, inspired. We want to make sure that everyone understands that they have a safe space. And I know that for myself, because when I was going through my journey as a previvor, it was important to know that people were surrounding me like community and I had someone that can understand and truly get what I was going through.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Community is so important. And I know, Dr. Peled, you're a surgeon, also a breast cancer survivor. When we talk about early detection, you want to focus on the importance of self-exams. It's something that we can all do.\par \par \uc2 DR ANNE PELED (BOARD MEMBER "THE BREASTIES")\par \par \uc2 For sure. And it's so important that we do breast self-exams because we need to know our normal. Because you don't know if you had a change if you don't know what your baseline is. And certainly, we know about 40% of breast cancers are actually found with lumps. And it's so important for early detection, better outcomes. And personally, I was doing breast self-exam because I found my own lump. And it's true to many of our breasties here. And a lot of us were so young, we weren't recommended to get screening mammograms yet. So, it's so key if you know how to do a good exam.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I told you when I had my radiologist, she actually took my hand and she goes, you never felt this? And the truth was, I didn't because I had never done a breast self-exam. So, you're going to show us how it's done on live television.\par \par \uc2 DR ANNE PELED (BOARD MEMBER "THE BREASTIES")\par \par \uc2 We're going to show you how to do it. So, one of things that's so important, we're all in clothes. But it's really important when you do this to not have any clothes on. And one of the things I tell people, try to do it if you can every month, same time every month.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRY DO IT MONTHLY & AT THE SAME TIME EVERY MONTH\par \par \uc2 DR ANNE PELED (BOARD MEMBER "THE BREASTIES")\par \par \uc2 So, the first thing you want to do is actually look at your breast. So, you want to look in the mirror. Put your hands on the hips. And actually look. Do you see any changes in your breast? How they look, any indentations. Did the nipples look different? Next, you want to actually move to the exam itself. So, you can do this in the shower, you can do it lying in bed.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAISE ONE HAND OVER YOUR HEAD, USE 3 FINGERS TO FEEL BREAST\par \par \uc2 DR ANNE PELED (BOARD MEMBER "THE BREASTIES")\par \par \uc2 You want to put one hand up over your head and you want to take the pads of your fingers, the three middle fingers and you want to put different levels of pressure. So, I like to talk about using a star, so you start on the sides, you're going to come in towards the middle of the breast, go down and about and just make sure that you're getting all the different parts of the breast.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: USE A CIRCULAR MOTION & APPLY DIFFERENT LEVELS OF PRESSURE\par \par \uc2 DR ANNE PELED (BOARD MEMBER "THE BREASTIES")\par \par \uc2 Then you actually want to go up underneath here, feel in your armpit. See if you feel any lumps.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER ALL OF THE BREAST, ARMPIT & UP COLLARBONE\par \par \uc2 DR ANNE PELED (BOARD MEMBER "THE BREASTIES")\par \par \uc2 And then, finally, get here by your clavicle, you're your collarbone. Really important to note that breast self-exams are not a substitute for imaging. So, even though it's incredibly important, you still, like you did, want to go in and get your mammograms, get MRIs.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VISUALLY EXAMINE YOUR BREAST TO LOOK FOR CHANGES\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And if you see something, you go to your doctor directly. Thank you all for being with us and to show everyone what we can do.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST SELF-EXAMS DO NOT REPLACE THE NEED FOR A MAMMOGRAM AS YOU GET OLDER\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's very much about empowerment and early detection. For more information about The Breasties, you can scan the QR code on your screen and we will be right back everyone. That was amazing.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 "Good Morning America" is sponsored by\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 What a great start.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221025eia30000r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NAVIGATING THE BREAST CANCER JOURNEY FRIENDS EMPHASIZING IMPORTANCE OF DOCTOR CHECK-INS\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE IAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR SURVIVORS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, BREKKE, DESANTIS, POWER OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, EVACUATION, DESANTIS, BECK, ANDERSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: QUESTIONS ABOUT FLORIDA'S EVACUATION ORDERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS UNDER FIRE AS LEE COUNTY DEATHS TOP 35\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, ZELENSKYY, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINE GAINS GROUND IN EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURROUNDED RUSSIAN TROOPS ABANDON CITY OF LYMAN\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, INVESTIGATION, INDONESIA\par \par \uc2 PRISONER EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SERIAL KILLER, CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES, ECONOMY, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAS PRICES APPROACHING NEW RECORD IN CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AVERAGE PRICE RISING BY $.71 IN THE PAST WEEK\par \par \uc2 MIDTERM ELECTIONS, KRANTZ, SEMENES, BOWHAN, OLSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ELECTION DAY NOW 36 DAYS AWAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON THE GROUND IN WISCONSIN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, RUSSIA, ANNEXATION, UKRAINE, ARCHIVES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, this is the start of Breast Cancer Awareness Month. And while the diagnosis is frightening one, it actually brought two longtime friends closer together.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NAVIGATING THE BREAST CANCER JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWO FRIENDS EMPHASIZING THE IMPORTANCE OF DOCTOR CHECK-INS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 2018, 35-year-old Sheryl Wall (PH) was diagnosed with breast cancer was diagnosed with breast cancer shortly after giving birth to her third child. She sought the guidance of her friend from the University of Alabama Birmingham Medical School, breast cancer specialist Dr. Erica Stringer-Reasor who was able to help Wall navigate her breast cancer journey. They both emphasized the importance of early screenings and checking with a doctor if you have any concerns at all saying, it can make all the difference.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that's why it's so important this month that we continue to talk about breast cancer awareness.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER AWARENESS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But still coming up here on "GMA," our Dr. Darien Sutton joining us with some important medical information to start Breast Cancer Awareness Month.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also, there's new fallout following that brutal on-field injury to rising star NFL Tua Tagovailoa. We'll be right back with more on that.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221021eia200034\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAST CANCER AWARENESS MONTH UNDERSTANDING THE IMPORTANCE OF MAMMOGRAMS\b0\par\par\uc2 880 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE IAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR SURVIVORS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, RESCUE, BREKKE, DESANTIS, POWER OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, EVACUATION, DESANTIS, BECK, ANDERSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: QUESTIONS ABOUT FLORIDA'S EVACUATION ORDERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS UNDER FIRE AS LEE COUNTY DEATHS TOP 35\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, ZELENSKYY, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINE GAINS GROUND IN EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURROUNDED RUSSIAN TROOPS ABANDON CITY OF LYMAN\par \par \uc2 STAMPEDE, INVESTIGATION, INDONESIA\par \par \uc2 PRISONER EXCHANGE, VENEZUELA\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SERIAL KILLER, CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GAS PRICES, ECONOMY, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAS PRICES APPROACHING NEW RECORD IN CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AVERAGE PRICE RISING BY $.71 IN THE PAST WEEK\par \par \uc2 MIDTERM ELECTIONS, KRANTZ, SEMENES, BOWHAN, OLSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ELECTION DAY NOW 36 DAYS AWAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON THE GROUND IN WISCONSIN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, RUSSIA, ANNEXATION, UKRAINE, ARCHIVES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 NASCAR, SAFETY, ELLIOTT, IWUJI, CRASH, NEXT GEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NASCAR DRIVERS RAISE SAFETY CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONTROVERSY OVER NEXT GENERATION CARS & TRUCKS AFTER MULTIPLE CRASHES\par \par \uc2 "POWER TRIP"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FRONT ROW SEAT TO MIDTERM ELECTIONS WITH "POWER TRIP"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCUSERIES FOLLOWS ABC NEWS REPORTERS ON THE CAMPAIGN TRAIL\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SALES, SHOPPING, BODGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EARLY BIRD GETS THE DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GETTING A HEAD START ON THE HOLIDAY DEALS\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, SCREENING, SYMPTOMS, TIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back. And "GMA Thriving in Pink," telling stories of courage and resilience all October long.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER AWARENESS MONTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNDERSTANDING THE IMPORTANCE OF MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Breast Cancer Awareness Month kicking off this weekend. And here with what to know and ask at your next cancer screening is ABC News medical contributor Dr. Darien Sutton joining us from Los Angeles. Dr. Sutton, you know we love having you. Let's start with cancer screenings. It seems like the importance of these screenings just can't be stressed enough.\par \par \uc2 DR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. Absolutely, Janai. Mammograms are the single most important screening method out there. They help to increase the chance of early detection and decrease the risk associated with breast cancer, including death. And according to \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2 , should start at or before the age of 45.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Dr. Sutton, okay, you know what, pretend like we're not on TV and I come to you and I say, hey, the next time I'm getting a screening, what are some of other health questions I should ask my doctor?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMPORTANT QUESTIONS TO ASK DURING A SCREENING\par \par \uc2 DR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Janai, I would recommend, first and foremost, that you have all of your information from any prior labs, imaging or screening tests. And this helps to create a good clinical picture of you who are. This, along with your family history and lifestyle choices also help to determine your individual risk, which may make you a candidate for additional screening tests such as genetic testing. I'd also recommend that when you get any test, to remember to ask when that test is going to result. If that results, who's going to contact with you with that result. And then, if it's abnormal, what would be the next step?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those are all good questions to remember when, who, what next. And when we talk about Breast Cancer Awareness Month, we put so much emphasis on women, obviously, but also men. They are part of this, too.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT MEN SHOULD KEEP IN MIND ABOUT BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 DR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. One out of every 100 cases of diagnosed breast cancer within the United States is diagnosed within men. And so, it's important that we're all aware of the symptoms, which can include but are not limited to lumps or swelling to the chest wall. Any changes in the skin to the chest, like irritation or changes in color or changes to the nipple. If you have any of these changes or symptoms, you should, at the very least, get evaluated by primary care physician.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It sounds like a small number, but so many people impacted. Dr. Sutton, thank you so much for being here with us. And coming up Monday on "GMA," a big surprise for women for raising breast cancer awareness and making a huge impact in their community. Plus, breast cancer in young people and how to be your own advocate. "GMA" is thriving in pink all month long. And we will be right back. Stick around.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Whit, can we get some Mickey Mouse before we go?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible), Eva.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hello.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you for joining us.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 He never (inaudible) thanks to me. Before we go, tomorrow's Monday night football matchup is an NFC west rivalry game between the Rams and the 49ers, a rematch of last season's NFC championship game. And who could forget, who could ever forget that?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 My 49ers, right. Oh, boy.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You set him up so good, Eva. I love it. Watch tomorrow night, 8:00 Eastern, 5:00 Pacific on \uc2 ESPN\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, gee, Goof.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221021eia20003a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RE-LAUNCHING "CANCER MOONSHOT" HOW INITIATIVE IMPACTS BREAST CANCER & OTHER RESEARCH\b0\par\par\uc2 734 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEATHER ALERT: COASTLINE CRUSHED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IAN CRUSHES NORTH AND SOUTH CAROLINA COASTLINES\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, LANDFALL\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, RUSSIA, UKRAINE, ANNEXATION, SANCTIONS\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, \uc2 NATO\uc2 , PIPELINE, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GANYARD, PUTIN, BIDEN, ANNEXATION, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 WALL STREET, FED, INTEREST, FOOD, ENERGY, HOUSING\par \par \uc2 MAYS, ACQUITTED, ARSON\par \par \uc2 JACKSON, INVESTITURE, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, BASEBALL, MANAGER\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP: "HOCUS POCUS 2"\par \par \uc2 DOLPHINS, TAGOVAILOA, SMITH, NINKOVICH, MCDANIEL, SILLS\par \par \uc2 "OPTIMUS", MUSK, HUMANOID, PROTOTYPE, BARR\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, TRAVEL, CHRISTMAS, THANKSGIVING, KELLY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEEKEND DOWNLOAD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE IAN, POWER OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RESCUE, ANIMALS, CANINE GLOBAL RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESCUING ANIMALS IN UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS ENTER WAR ZONE TO SAVE CATS & DOGS\par \par \uc2 LISTERIA, SAFETY, OUTBREAK, RECALL, CHEESE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LISTERIA OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CDC ISSUES WARNING, 20 CHEESE BRANDS BEING RECALLED\par \par \uc2 OSBOURNE, LEVIN, GESTATIONAL DIABETES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, CARDINAL, EMANUEL, CANCER MOONSHOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to Breast Cancer Awareness Month kicking off this October 1st. And "GMA" is thriving in pink telling stories of courage and resilience all month long.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. This morning, a look at the Cancer Moonshot Initiative out of the White House. President Biden setting big goals in advancements in cancer treatment. MaryAlice Parks is in Washington with more. MaryAlice, good morning.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, good morning. President Biden has been committed to cancer research. And yesterday, he also put out a proclamation about Breast Cancer Awareness Month, urging the country to come together to support patients and survivors, to pay tribute to those who have died and, of course, to continue to get the word out about screenings.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RE-LAUNCHING "CANCER MOONSHOT"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW INITIATIVE IMPACTS BREAST CANCER & OTHER RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, as Breast Cancer Awareness Month begins, the White House aiming to tackle all cancer as we know it.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 It's bold. It's ambitious, but it is completely doable. The goal is to cut the cancer death rate in half in the next 25 years at least by 50%.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Arguably, the goal closest to the President's heart after losing his son Beau to brain cancer, then President Biden lunching the Cancer Moonshot Initiative in 2016, doubling down and reigniting the program this year, declaring that curing cancer was a presidential White House priority.\par \par \uc2 DR DANIELLE CARNIVAL (WHITE HOUSE CANCER MOONSHOT COORDINATOR)\par \par \uc2 It really started a movement of, if we work together, if we share more data, if we do this together, we can actually make progress in a new way.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, the Cancer Moonshot has spent over $1.5 billion on cancer prevention, technologies and even...\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26for cancers. But prevention and inequalities in the health care system remain a problem.\par \par \uc2 DR EZEKIEL EMANUEL (VICE PROVOST OF GLOBAL INITIATIVES UNIV OF PA)\par \par \uc2 We know we have these capacities to cure patients. And yet either because of insurance or where they live or the fact that they don't have a regular doctor and didn't get screened, they show up with much advanced cancers that we really can't do, we can't cure. That's terribly tragic.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Zeke Manuel, a former health adviser to President Obama, says increased access to insurance and information will better help people prevent cancers moving forward. He says it will take a holistic approach that, like landing on the moon, there is no quick fix to fighting cancer, only a worthwhile mission.\par \par \uc2 DR EZEKIEL EMANUEL (VICE PROVOST OF GLOBAL INITIATIVES UNIV OF PA)\par \par \uc2 All of us wish it were a silver bullet, but the moonshot was not a silver bullet either. It required, you know, almost ten years of hard work bringing hundreds of thousands of people together to do things that had never been done before.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It was interesting talking to some of these doctors who do seem so excited by some of the cutting-edge research. Science that could someday harness the body's own immune system to fight cancer. Clearly, just a lot of very cool work being done to try and save lives. Eva?\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, very cool work. Thank you so much, MaryAlice.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221024eia10000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FIGHT OVER REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS ARIZONA JUDGE UPHOLDS CENTURY OLD ABORTION LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 620 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TROPICAL STORM IAN, WEATHER, TRACK, BRENNAN, EVATT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, TROPICAL STORM IAN\par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, MISSILE TEST, SOUTH KOREA, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTH KOREA TEST-FIRES SHORT-RANGE MISSILE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. AIRCRAFT CARRIER ARRIVES IN SOUTH KOREA FOR MILITARY EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, INVASION, PROTESTS, DRAFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS BREAK OUT IN RUSSIA OVER WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS HIT THE STREETS IN OVER 30 CITIES; MORE THAN 700 ARRESTED\par \par \uc2 ELECTIONS, HOBBS, ABORTION, BAN, DEADRICK, MAYES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIGHT OVER REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA JUDGE UPHOLDS CENTURY OLD ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to politics and the battle over abortion rights. As the midterm election approaches, Arizona now enacting a ban on abortions after 15 weeks, just a day after a judge upheld a century-old law that jails abortion providers. ABC's MaryAlice Parks joins us now with more. Good morning, MaryAlice.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Erielle, good morning. Yeah, in several key states, early and mail-in voting is already underway. But this weekend, it is the issue of abortion access back front and center in some of those crucial battleground states, including Arizona.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just over six weeks until Election Day, a new law in Arizona going into effect this weekend signed by the Republican governor banning abortion after 15 weeks of a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 KAREN DEADRICK (REPUBLICAN ARIZONA VOTER)\par \par \uc2 You don't like your state laws on abortion, go somewhere else.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But that new law coming just a day after an Arizona judge said an even more restrictive near total abortion ban on the books since 1901 should also be reinstated.\par \par \uc2 KRIS MAYES (ARIZONA ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 Women and girls will die because of it.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Democratic candidates blasting the decision.\par \par \uc2 KATIE HOBBS (SECRETARY OF STATE OF ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 I'm furious that my 20-year-old daughter will have fewer rights than I did 50 years ago.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On the ground, chaos and confusion for doctors and patients as state officials disagree about which law should take precedence.\par \par \uc2 BRITTANY FONTENO (PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 We had abortion appointments booked up for the rest of the month and our providers had to make those really difficult, really traumatic phone calls to cancel those appointments.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INDIANA JUDGE ISSUES PRELIMINARY INJUNCTION ON RESTRICTIVE BAN\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Indiana, abortion clinics now reopening after a judge there put a pause on a new restrictive ban just a week after it had gone into effect.\par \par \uc2 DR KATIE MCHUGH (ABORTION PLANNER)\par \par \uc2 This judge is responding to the need of people to what she believes is a constitutional protection to privacy. And this health care decision falls within that constitutional protection.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN VOTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC NEWS/WASHINGTON POST POLL: 64% OPPOSE SUPREME COURT RULING\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to our new ABC News/"Washington Post" poll, across the country, a vast majority of voters oppose the recent Supreme Court decision eliminating the constitutional right to an abortion. Our poll also found that Americans trust Democrats on the issue over Republicans by a 20-point margin.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHTS TO ABORTION\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have seen Democrats trying to turn out voters on this issue of abortion access. Republicans on the campaign trail have largely shied away from this issue. But this is important. Our poll also found that the economy, crime, inflation and education were top of the list on voters' minds right now, 84% in our poll have said that the economy was important in their vote. Janai?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is a huge number. MaryAlice, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221014ei9p0002y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FIGHT OVER REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS POLL: AMERICANS OPPOSE ROE V WADE RULING\b0\par\par\uc2 862 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TROPICAL STORM IAN, WEATHER, TRACK, BRENNAN, EVATT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, TROPICAL STORM IAN\par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, MISSILE TEST, SOUTH KOREA, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTH KOREA TEST-FIRES SHORT-RANGE MISSILE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. AIRCRAFT CARRIER ARRIVES IN SOUTH KOREA FOR MILITARY EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, INVASION, PROTESTS, DRAFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS BREAK OUT IN RUSSIA OVER WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS HIT THE STREETS IN OVER 30 CITIES; MORE THAN 700 ARRESTED\par \par \uc2 ELECTIONS, HOBBS, ABORTION, BAN, DEADRICK, MAYES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIGHT OVER REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA JUDGE UPHOLDS CENTURY OLD ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, ECONOMY, INFLATION, MIDTERMS, POLL\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And to talk more on those points, on politics, we welcome ABC's congressional correspondent Rachel Scott. Rachel, you know, how much we love having you here in person. Abortion is a big issue.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLL: AMERICANS OPPOSE ROE V WADE RULING\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But as MaryAlice has laid out, economy, inflation top of mind for many voters, 84% saying the economy is important. That's a point of a lot of criticism of President Biden and his handling of those issues.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN'S APPROVAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY ISSUES INTO PRESIDENT'S RATING\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Janai, it is the top two issues for voters when we did this poll just out today. And this is a big challenge for Democrats and they know it. According to our latest poll, 74% of Americans see the economy in bad shape. Inflation is at a 40-year high. You have Americans paying more at the gas pump, at the grocery store. And then on top of that, you have more registered voters saying that they trust Republicans on the issue over Democrats. The President's approval ratings are low. When we go back and we look at history here, when presidents have an approval rating as low as this president, under 40%, they lose on average 37 seats in the midterm election.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow. And so, that would lead many to think that this works in favor of Republicans. Back to the issue of abortion, that new poll shows, as MaryAlice said, Americans overwhelmingly oppose the Supreme Court overturning Roe v. Wade. You've done incredible reporting on the issue. That's going to be a driving force for many voters with the bans that we're seeing in places like Arizona. Is that enough to change the tide one way or the another?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and I think Democrats here are hoping that that outrage that we're seeing in our poll turns into energy, political energy, that it mobilizes people to get to the polls. And though we have seen clues, we've seen signs that it is a defining issue for voters. The conservative state of Kansas overwhelmingly voted to protect abortion rights earlier this summer. Right here in New York City, you had a critical special election in a swing district. The Democrat there campaigning on the issue of abortion. He ended up churning out a victory. But still, looking at our poll here, abortion does fall lower when registered voters are asked what issues are most important to them.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Are most important. Okay. And changing gears now, Rachel, the January 6th committee set to hold another hearing this week.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JANUARY 6TH RIOTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW COULD IT IMPACT THE MIDTERMS?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) After the hearings over the summer, do you get the sense that Americans are paying attention? And what impact, if any, could this have on the midterms 40 days plus out?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and it is expected to be the final hearing before the midterm elections coming up this week. It's clear that Americans are paying attention not only to these hearings, but also to the investigation surrounding the former president. A slim majority say that Trump should be charged with a crime. But Republicans appear to be split on whether or not he should run in 2024. But make no mistake about it, Trump still does have a hold on this Republican Party, especially when it comes to his false claims about the 2020 election. FiveThirtyEight shows that 60% of Americans will have an election denier on the ballot this November.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow, a lot of big headlines in politics. Rachel, we still appreciate you having you here.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good to be here.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) and tune in on "This Week" later this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS MORNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAKE SULLIVAN, WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL SECURITY ADVISER\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) George Stephanopoulos will go one-on-one with President Biden's national security adviser Jake Sullivan about the war in Ukraine and those major protests across Iran.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEN. \uc2 JOHN BARRASSO\uc2  (REP), WYOMING\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, George has an exclusive interview with Senate Republican conference chair \uc2 John Barrasso\uc2  on immigration and the economy with less than six weeks until the midterm elections. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Janai, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221014ei9p0002z\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/30/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdr